msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Sprinting"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>At the cost of your fatigue, you can travel quicker with "
"sprinting.</>\n"
"\n"
"Sprint <IA id=\"IA_Game_Movement_Sprint\"/>\n"
"\n"
"As you sprint, your fatigue will gradually decrease. If your fatigue runs "
"out, you can no longer sprint and will move at your normal running speed "
"until your fatigue regenerates. It is also notheworthy that you can only "
"sprint forward and not on the side or backward."
msgstr ""

msgctxt ""
"ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Blocking&FatigueManagement"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Attacking, jumping, sprinting or blocking</> consumes your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Fatigue</>. \n"
"\n"
"Some actions, like <RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</>, can only be perfomed if you "
"have <RT_BlueMed>enough Fatigue</>. \n"
"\n"
"Opponents can also decrease your Fatigue with <RT_BlueMed>spells or "
"attacks</>. Make sure they don't deplete your Fatigue or you might be thrown "
"<RT_BlueMed>off balance</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Physical attacks</> that deplete your Fatigue, such as blocking "
"an attack, will briefly <RT_BlueMed>stagger</> you.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Magical effects</> that deplete your Fatigue will "
"<RT_BlueMed>knock you down</>.\n"
"\n"
"When enemies are <RT_BlueMed>almost out of Fatigue</>, their <RT_BlueMed>life "
"indicator will pulse</>. This is a good moment to try and break their balance."
msgstr ""

msgctxt ""
"ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_CharacterSkillPerks_Description_SpeechcraftExpert"
msgid "<RT_BlueMed>Bribes</> cost <RT_BlueMed>much less</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_LockpickingController"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Doors and containers</> like chests are sometimes locked, "
"preventing you from opening them.\n"
"\n"
"To pick a lock open, make sure to have <RT_BlueMed>Lockpicks</> on you when "
"interacting with the lock.\n"
"\n"
"A <RT_BlueMed>side view</> of the the lock will appear. Use your lockpick to "
"<RT_BlueMed>push</> any <RT_BlueMed>loose tumbler</> up and press <IA "
"id=\"IA_UI_Generic_Accept\"/> to <RT_BlueMed>set</> them in place as they "
"<RT_BlueMed>reach the top</>.\n"
"\n"
"Pressing <IA id=\"IA_UI_Generic_Accept\"/> <RT_BlueMed>too soon, too late</> "
"or when the tumbler is <RT_BlueMed>moving too fast</> will cause the tumbler "
"to snap back and <RT_BlueMed>break</> the lockpick.\n"
"It may also cause <RT_BlueMed>other lodged tumblers</> to <RT_BlueMed>fall</> "
"along with it.\n"
"\n"
"As your Security Skill increases, tumblers move more slowly and fewer "
"tumblers drop when you fail.\n"
"\n"
"Locks come in <RT_BlueMed>five difficulty grades</>; the higher the grade, "
"the harder they are to pick. Some locks are <RT_BlueMed>impossible</> to pick "
"and <RT_BlueMed>require a key</>.\n"
"\n"
"If you are <RT_BlueMed>having difficulties</> picking the lock, you can use "
"the <RT_BlueMed>\"Auto Attempt\"</> option. It automatically checks the "
"difficulty of the lock against your Security Skill, and calculates the "
"<RT_BlueMed>odds of successfully picking the lock</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Lockpicking"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Doors and containers</> like chests are sometimes locked, "
"preventing you from opening them.\n"
"\n"
"To pick a lock open, make sure to have <RT_BlueMed>Lockpicks</> on you when "
"interacting with the lock.\n"
"\n"
"A <RT_BlueMed>side view</> of the the lock will appear. Use your lockpick to "
"<RT_BlueMed>push</> any <RT_BlueMed>loose tumbler</> up and press <IA "
"id=\"IA_UI_Specific_LockPickMenu_SetTumbler\"/> to <RT_BlueMed>set</> them in "
"place as they <RT_BlueMed>reach the top</>.\n"
"\n"
"Pressing <IA id=\"IA_UI_Specific_LockPickMenu_SetTumbler\"/> <RT_BlueMed>too "
"soon, too late</> or when the tumbler is <RT_BlueMed>moving too fast</> will "
"cause the tumbler to snap back and <RT_BlueMed>break</> the lockpick.\n"
"It may also cause <RT_BlueMed>other lodged tumblers</> to <RT_BlueMed>fall</> "
"along with it.\n"
"\n"
"As your Security Skill increases, tumblers move more slowly and fewer "
"tumblers drop when you fail.\n"
"\n"
"Locks come in <RT_BlueMed>five difficulty grades</>; the higher the grade, "
"the harder they are to pick. Some locks are <RT_BlueMed>impossible</> to pick "
"and <RT_BlueMed>require a key</>.\n"
"\n"
"If you are <RT_BlueMed>having difficulties</> picking the lock, you can use "
"the <RT_BlueMed>\"Auto Attempt\"</> option. It automatically checks the "
"difficulty of the lock against your Security Skill, and calculates the "
"<RT_BlueMed>odds of successfully picking the lock</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Fame&Infamy"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Fame</> is a trait that measures your <RT_BlueMed>heroism</>. You "
"can increase it by <RT_BlueMed>helping people</> or completing quests in a "
"<RT_BlueMed>virtuous manner</>.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Fame</> increases <RT_BlueMed>people’s Disposition</> toward "
"you.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Infamy</> is the opposite of Fame. It measures how infamous you "
"are for your <RT_BlueMed>misdeeds</> and "
"<RT_BlueMed>crimes</>.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Infamy</> makes you <RT_BlueMed>unable to pray at Altars of the "
"Nine Divines</>, making it more difficult to get rid of diseases.\n"
"\n"
"High Fame or high Infamy are sometimes required to <RT_BlueMed>start specific "
"quests</>.\n"
"\n"
"You can find your Fame and Infamy in the <RT_BlueMed>Details page</> of the "
"Character section of the journal."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_CustomClass_InfoBox_FavoredAttributes"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Favored attributes</> receive an initial <RT_BlueMed>+5 bonus</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_CustomClass_InfoBox_MajorSkills"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Major skills</> receive an initial <RT_BlueMed>+20 level bonus</> "
"and <RT_BlueMed>increase much more rapidly</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt ""
"ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_CharacterSkillPerks_Description_SecurityMaster"
msgid "<RT_BlueMed>No tumblers fall</> when you fail and break a lockpick."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Staves"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Staves</> are magical conduits that allow you to cast "
"<RT_BlueMed>spells without consuming any Magicka</>. \n"
"\n"
"Like enchanted weapons, they can only be used a <RT_BlueMed>limited number of "
"times</> before needing to be <RT_BlueMed>recharged</>. \n"
"\n"
"Like any weapon, they can be equipped through the inventory. However, unlike "
"other weapons, you <RT_BlueMed>cannot use them to deal physical "
"damage</>.\n"
"\n"
"There are a lot of different staves with different spells tied to them. You "
"can wield and use any staff, no matter your Skills."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Swimming"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>To swim forward and backwards</>, press <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Movement_MovementForward\"/> and <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Movement_MovementBackward\"/>.\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>swim sideways</>, press <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Movement_MovementLeft\"/> and <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Movement_MovementRight\"/>.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Looking down</> makes your character <RT_BlueMed>go "
"underwater</>, while <RT_BlueMed>looking up</> makes your character "
"<RT_BlueMed>go towards the surface</>.\n"
"\n"
"Pay attention to the <RT_BlueMed>breath meter</> that appears when you are "
"underwater.\n"
"If it depletes, you will start to <RT_BlueMed>drown</> and will "
"<RT_BlueMed>very quickly lose Health</> over time.\n"
"\n"
"You can still <RT_BlueMed>swing a weapon</> or <RT_BlueMed>use your fists</> "
"underwater, but you <RT_BlueMed>cannot perform Power Attacks</>. In addition, "
"<RT_BlueMed>arrows are much less effective</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Notifications"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>When an event happens, a notification appears on the top left of "
"the screen showing the details of that action.</>\n"
"They can appear in the HUD as well as in your inventory to indicate a new "
"item was added or removed, for instance.\n"
"They are displayed for three seconds before disappearing or switching to the "
"following notified event."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Vitals"
msgid ""
"<img id=\"Health\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Health</> is the amount of <RT_BlueMed>damage you can take before "
"you die</>. It increases every time you <RT_BlueMed>level up</>. \n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Endurance</> greatly affects your total Health and how quickly "
"it regenerates.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Strength</> also slightly affects your total Health.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Magicka\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Magicka</> is used to <RT_BlueMed>cast spells</>. The stronger "
"the spell, the more Magicka it costs.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Intelligence</> affects your total Magicka.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Willpower</> affects how quickly you regenerate "
"Magicka.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Fatigue\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Fatigue</> represents the amount of actions you can do before "
"being <RT_BlueMed>tired and vunerable</>.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Willpower</> greatly affects your total Fatigue.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Agility</> also slightly affects your total Fatigue and how "
"quickly it regenerates.\n"
"\n"
"You can <RT_BlueMed>sleep, wait, drink potions or use spells</> to quickly "
"restore your Vitals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_MagicItems"
msgid ""
"<img id=\"MagicScroll\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• SCROLLS •</>\n"
"Scrolls are spells that <RT_BlueMed>can only be cast once</> but without "
"needing a specific Skill level.\n"
"To equip a scroll, select it from either the Inventory or the Magic section "
"of the journal.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"VarlaStone\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• VARLA STONES •</>\n"
"Varla Stones are enchanted shards of meteoric glass, usually found atop "
"pedestals in Ayleid ruins.\n"
"They can be used to <RT_BlueMed>recharge all enchanted items</> in your "
"inventory, destroying themselves in the process.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"WelkyndStone\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• WELKYND STONES •</>\n"
"Welkynd Stones are glowing magical stones created by the Ayleids as a means "
"of storing Magicka.\n"
"They can be used to <RT_BlueMed>completely restore all your Magicka</>, "
"destroying themselves in the process.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"SigilStone\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• SIGIL STONES •</>\n"
"Sigil Stones are powerful Daedric artifacts found in the Planes of "
"Oblivion.\n"
"They can be used to <RT_BlueMed>enchant any weapon or equipment</>, "
"destroying themselves in the process."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_MagicItems "
msgid ""
"<img id=\"MagicScroll\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>MAGIC SCROLLS</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Magical scrolls can be cast like a spell.</> They can only be "
"used once, and are destroyed when they are cast. To ready a scroll as your "
"Active Magic, select it from your Magic menu. In the Inventory, the detail "
"page indicates a scroll’s spell effects.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"VarlaStone\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>VARLA STONES</>\n"
"Use Varla Stones to <RT_BlueMed>recharge all magical items in your inventory "
"at once</>. To use Varla Stones, select them in your Inventory. The stone is "
"destroyed on use.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"WelkyndStone\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>WELKYND STONES</>\n"
"Welkynd Stones <RT_BlueMed>restore your Magicka to its maximum</>. To use "
"Welkynd Stones, select them in your Inventory. The stone is destroyed on "
"use.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"SigilStone\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>SIGIL STONES</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>These exotic products of Daedric magic produce enchanted "
"items.</> To use Sigil Stones, select them in your Inventory.\n"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Dodging"
msgid ""
"A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> in <RT_BlueMed>Acrobatics</> gains the ability to "
"<RT_BlueMed>Dodge</>. \n"
"\n"
"To Dodge, <RT_BlueMed>simultaneously</> press <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Block\"/> and <IA id=\"IA_Game_Movement_Jump\"/> "
"<RT_BlueMed>while moving</>. \n"
"\n"
"Dodging is useful to quickly get in and out of melee combat, and can make it "
"easier to <RT_BlueMed>avoid projectiles</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_System_BodyText_MandatoryUpdate"
msgid ""
"A mandatory update is required to proceed. Please make sure you are connected "
"to the internet and restart the game in order to continue playing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Haggling"
msgid ""
"A merchant <RT_BlueMed>might be open</> to selling at a lower price or buying "
"at a higher price, but the extent of their <RT_BlueMed>flexibility</> can "
"only be discovered through <RT_BlueMed>haggling</>.\n"
"\n"
"When haggling, the merchant's Mercantile mastery and current Disposition "
"towards you is displayed.\n"
"\n"
"Using this information, it is up to you to define <RT_BlueMed>how far you "
"want to push</> the haggling.\n"
"\n"
"If the merchant has a <RT_BlueMed>good opinion</> of you, you can probably "
"try to push the slider a bit <RT_BlueMed>to the right</>.\n"
"But if you're <RT_BlueMed>not as skilled</> in Mercantile as that merchant, "
"you <RT_BlueMed>shouldn't push too far</>.\n"
"\n"
"When you next try to buy or sell an item, the merchant <RT_BlueMed>may refuse "
"the deal</>. If they do, their <RT_BlueMed>Disposition</> towards you will "
"<RT_BlueMed>decrease</>. If they don't, it's up to you to try to haggle even "
"more.\n"
"Once a merchant accepts a deal, they will generally <RT_BlueMed>continue to "
"accept</> other offers at the same haggle value, unless their Disposition "
"towards you changed."
msgstr ""

