msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Spellcrafting"
msgid ""
"After advancing the ranks of the <RT_BlueMed>Mages Guild</>, you will be "
"allowed into the prestigious Arcane University, and will discover one of its "
"most powerful benefits: <RT_BlueMed>creating custom spells</>. \n"
"\n"
"Custom spells can only be made at an <RT_BlueMed>Altar of Spellmaking</>. Two "
"are located at the Praxographical Center building, at the <RT_BlueMed>Arcane "
"University</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"SpellmakingAltar\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"The Altar allows you to create spells tailored to your needs by allowing you "
"to <RT_BlueMed>combine multiple magic effects</> into a single "
"spell.\n"
"However, you can only create spells with <RT_BlueMed>magic effects you "
"know</> and are able to cast according to your <RT_BlueMed>Skill "
"level</>.\n"
"\n"
"When creating spells, most effects have <RT_BlueMed>three parameters</> that "
"must be determined, altough some only have a few:\n"
"• The <RT_BlueMed>Magnitude</> defines <RT_BlueMed>the power of the "
"effect</>.\n"
"• The <RT_BlueMed>Duration</> defines <RT_BlueMed>the amount of time the "
"effect lasts</>.\n"
"• The <RT_BlueMed>Area</> defines <RT_BlueMed>the size of the area of "
"effect</> around the target.\n"
"\n"
"In addition, most effects have <RT_BlueMed>three range options</>:\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Touch</> applies the spell to the nearest creature or character "
"within <RT_BlueMed>close range</>.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Target</> applies the spell on a creature or character using a "
"<RT_BlueMed>long distance projectile</>.\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Self</> applies the spell’s effects to <RT_BlueMed>you "
"only</>.\n"
"\n"
"Increasing any of the parameters will affect both the <RT_BlueMed>power</> "
"and the <RT_BlueMed>cost</> of the spell.\n"
"You cannot craft a spell if you do not have the <RT_BlueMed>required Magicka "
"and Skill level</> to cast it.\n"
"\n"
"Of course, don't forget to give your spell a <RT_BlueMed>nice fitting name</>."
msgstr ""

