msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_ItemDurability"
msgid ""
"As armor pieces get hit and weapons are used, their <RT_BlueMed>durability "
"decreases</>.\n"
"\n"
"Items <RT_BlueMed>break</> and become less effective when their durability "
"<RT_BlueMed>drops to 0</>. Broken weapons deal 50% less damage. Broken armor "
"pieces provide 75% less protection.\n"
"\n"
"You can see the durability of a weapon or armor in your inventory:\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"BrokenWeapon\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"If you possess <RT_BlueMed>Repair Hammers</>, you can use them to "
"<RT_BlueMed>repair equipments yourself</>. Doing so improves your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Armorer skill</>.\n"
"Otherwise, you can <RT_BlueMed>pay merchants</> to have your equipment "
"repaired.\n"
"\n"
"When your equipped weapon or armor pieces are broken or about to break, icons "
"appear next to your Vitals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Ingredients"
msgid ""
"As you <RT_BlueMed>roam around the world</> and fight <RT_BlueMed>all sorts "
"of creatures</>, you may stumble upon various ingredients.\n"
"These ingredients can be used to <RT_BlueMed>create potions and poisons</>, "
"but can also be <RT_BlueMed>consumed directly</>. When consumed, only their "
"<RT_BlueMed>first effect</> is granted to you.\n"
"\n"
"As your <RT_BlueMed>Alchemy skill improves</>, you will be able to "
"<RT_BlueMed>recognize more effects</>. An Apprentice only recognizes two out "
"of the four effects, but an Expert recognizes all four.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Inventory_IngredientEffect\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"Most ingredients have <RT_BlueMed>four effects</>, but you may stumble upon a "
"few that only sport <RT_BlueMed>a single powerful one</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_CombatSkills"
msgid ""
"As you reach <RT_BlueMed>specific milestones</> within a skill, you will "
"<RT_BlueMed>gain its associated perks</>. This section details the combat-"
"related skills and perks.\n"
" \n"
"<img id=\"Blade\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• BLADE •</>\n"
"The Blade Skill affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with "
"<RT_BlueMed>Blade weapons</>, such as Daggers, Shortswords, Longswords and "
"Claymores.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> has no particular perk.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</>'s Power Attacks deal 20% more damage, and "
"their weapons are 20% more durable.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</>'s Power Attacks apply a 15% Weakness to Normal "
"Weapons for 5 seconds.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</>'s Regular Attacks have a 20% chance to make the "
"target Bleed for 3 seconds.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</>'s Power Attacks apply a 30% Weakness to Normal "
"Weapons for 10 seconds.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Blade, hit your opponents with "
"<RT_BlueMed>Daggers, Shortswords, Longswords or Claymores</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Blunt\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• BLUNT •</>\n"
"The Blunt Skill affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you do with "
"<RT_BlueMed>Blunt weapons</>, such as War Axes, Maces, Battle-Axes and "
"Warhammers.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> has no particular perk.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</>'s Power Attacks deal 20% more damage, and "
"their weapons are 20% more durable.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</>'s Power Attacks grant 15% Shield for 5 seconds. "
"\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</>'s Regular Attacks have a 20% chance to apply "
"Silence for 10 seconds. \n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</>'s Power Attacks grant 30% Shield for 10 seconds. "
"\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Blunt, hit your opponents with "
"<RT_BlueMed>War Axes, Maces, Battle-Axes or Warhammers</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"HandToHand\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• HAND-TO-HAND •</>\n"
"The Hand-To-Hand Skill affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you do with "
"your <RT_BlueMed>bare hands</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</>'s attacks additionally deal Fatigue damage equal to "
"50% of their Health damage. They do not recoil armed opponents when blocking "
"their attacks.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</>'s Power Attacks deal 20% more damage, and they "
"always recoil their opponents when blocking.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</>'s Power Attacks have a 25% chance to disarm "
"their opponents.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</>'s attacks deal Fatigue damage equal to 75% of "
"their Health Damage.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</>'s attacks deal Fatigue damage equal to 100% of "
"their Health Damage.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Hand-to-hand, hit your opponents "
"with your <RT_BlueMed>bare fists</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Block\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• BLOCK •</>\n"
"The Block Skill affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you "
"<RT_BlueMed>mitigate</> when blocking an attack.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</>'s shield or weapon lose durability when blocking an "
"attack.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</>'s shield or weapon no longer lose durability "
"when blocking an attack.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> consumes 25% less Fatigue when blocking an "
"attack.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> consumes 50% less Fatigue when blocking an attack, "
"and can perform a Shield Bash that staggers their opponents. \n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> consumes 75% less Fatigue when blocking an attack "
"and deals 150% more damage when they Shield Bash.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Block, <RT_BlueMed>block</> your "
"opponents attacks.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Armorer\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• ARMORER •</>\n"
"The Armorer Skill affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>maintain weapons and "
"armor at top efficiency</>. Broken weapons and armor are much less "
"effective.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> cannot repair magic items.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can repair magic items.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</>'s Repair Hammers last twice as long.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can repair items beyond their highest condition, "
"up to 125%. Improved weapons do extra damage, improved armors protect "
"more.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> never breaks Repair Hammers. One hammer lasts a "
"lifetime.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Armorer, <RT_BlueMed>repair</> your "
"weapons and gear using Repair Hammers.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"HeavyArmor\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• HEAVY ARMOR •</>\n"
"The Heavy Armor Skill affects your ability to use <RT_BlueMed>Heavy armors</> "
"more effectively.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</>'s Heavy Armor degrades 50% faster.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</>'s Heavy Armor degrades at a normal rate.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</>'s Heavy Armor degrades 50% slower.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</>'s equipped Heavy Armor only encumbers them by "
"50%.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</>'s equipped Heavy Armor does not encumber them at "
"all.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Heavy Armor, <RT_BlueMed>get hit</> "
"while wearing Heavy Armor gear.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Athletics\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• ATHLETICS •</>\n"
"The Athletics Skill affects how quickly you <RT_BlueMed>run, swim and "
"sprint</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> regenerates their Fatigue 25% more slowly when "
"running.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> regenerates their Fatigue at a normal rate "
"when running.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> consumes 30% less Fatigue while sprinting.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> consumes 60% less Fatigue while sprinting.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> no longer consumes any Fatigue while sprinting. "
"\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Athletics, <RT_BlueMed>run, sprint "
"or swim</> great distances."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_MagicSkills"
msgid ""
"As you reach <RT_BlueMed>specific milestones</> within a skill, you will "
"<RT_BlueMed>gain its associated perks</>. This section details the magic-"
"related skills and perks.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Destruction\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• DESTRUCTION •</>\n"
"The Destruction Skill reduces the amount of Magicka required to cast spells "
"to <RT_BlueMed>inflict elemental damage</> and <RT_BlueMed>weaken</> your "
"opponents.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> can only cast Novice level Destruction spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can cast Apprentice level Destruction "
"spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can cast Journeyman level Destruction "
"spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can cast Expert level Destruction spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> can cast all Destruction spells.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Destruction, <RT_BlueMed>cast "
"Destruction spells</> on a valid target.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Restoration\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• RESTORATION •</>\n"
"The Restoration Skill reduces the amount of Magicka required to cast spells "
"to <RT_BlueMed>restore, fortify and absorb attributes, cure diseases</>, and "
"<RT_BlueMed>improve resistances</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> can only cast Novice level Restoration spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can cast Apprentice level Restoration "
"spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can cast Journeyman level Restoration "
"spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can cast Expert level Restoration spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> can cast all Restoration spells.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Restoration, <RT_BlueMed>cast "
"Restoration spells</> on a valid target.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Conjuration\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• CONJURATION •</>\n"
"The Conjuration Skill reduces the amount of Magicka required to cast spells "
"to <RT_BlueMed>summon</> creatures, weapons and armor, and <RT_BlueMed>turn "
"the undead</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> can only cast Novice level Conjuration spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can cast Apprentice level Conjuration "
"spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can cast Journeyman level Conjuration "
"spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can cast Expert level Conjuration spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> can cast all Conjuration spells.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Conjuration, <RT_BlueMed>cast "
"Conjuration spells</> on a valid target.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Illusion\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• ILLUSION •</>\n"
"The Illusion Skill reduces the amount of Magicka required to cast spells to "
"<RT_BlueMed>charm, conceal, create light, silence, paralyze, command</> and "
"<RT_BlueMed>affect aggressivity</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> can only cast Novice level Illusion spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can cast Apprentice level Illusion spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can cast Journeyman level Illusion spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can cast Expert level Illusion spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> can cast all Illusion spells.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Illusion, <RT_BlueMed>cast Illusion "
"spells</> on a valid target.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Alteration\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• ALTERATION •</>\n"
"The Alteration Skill reduces the amount of Magicka required to cast spells to "
"<RT_BlueMed>breathe or walk on water, open locks, reduce encumbrance</>, and "
"<RT_BlueMed>shield yourself</> from physical and magical damage.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> can only cast Novice level Alteration spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can cast Apprentice level Alteration "
"spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can cast Journeyman level Alteration spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can cast Expert level Alteration spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> can cast all Alteration spells.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Alteration, <RT_BlueMed>cast "
"Alteration spells</> on a valid target.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Mysticism\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• MYSTICISM •</>\n"
"The Mysticism Skill reduces the amount of Magicka required to cast spells to "
"<RT_BlueMed>absorb magic, reflect damage, dispel, move objects, sense life, "
"reveal paths</> and <RT_BlueMed>bind souls</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> can only cast Novice level Mysticism spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can cast Apprentice level Mysticism spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can cast Journeyman level Mysticism spells.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can cast Expert level Mysticism spells.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> can cast all Mysticism spells.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Mysticism, <RT_BlueMed>cast "
"Mysticism spells</> on a valid target.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Alchemy\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• ALCHEMY •</>\n"
"The Alchemy Skill affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>create potions</> and "
"<RT_BlueMed>obtain greater benefits</> from alchemical ingredients.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> recognizes only the first alchemical property of a "
"substance, and can only handle 4 simultaneous potion effects.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> recognizes the first two alchemical properties "
"of a substance, and has a 25% chance to craft an additional potion.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> recognizes three alchemical properties of a "
"substance, and can handle 6 simultaneous potion effects.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> recognizes all four alchemical properties of a "
"substance, and always crafts an additional potion.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> can make potions from a single ingredient, and can "
"handle 10 simultaneous potion effects.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Alchemy, <RT_BlueMed>eat "
"ingredients</> or <RT_BlueMed>create potions and poisons</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_StealthSkills"
msgid ""
"As you reach <RT_BlueMed>specific milestones</> within a skill, you will "
"<RT_BlueMed>gain its associated perks</>. This section details the stealth-"
"related skills and perks.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Marksman\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• MARKSMAN •</>\n"
"The Marksman Skill affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with "
"<RT_BlueMed>Bows</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> loses Fatigue while aiming.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> no longer loses Fatigue while aiming.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can focus their vision by holding down <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Block\"/> while aiming.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</>'s arrows have a 10% chance to paralyze the target "
"for 5 seconds on hit.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</>'s arrows have a 25% chance to paralyze the target "
"for 5 seconds on hit.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Marksman, hit your opponents with "
"<RT_BlueMed>arrows</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Sneak\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• SNEAK •</>\n"
"The Sneak Skill affects your ability to deal <RT_BlueMed>extra damage</> when "
"attacking <RT_BlueMed>undetected, pick pockets</> and <RT_BlueMed>move unseen "
"and unheard</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</>'s Sneak Attacks with a Dagger deal 5 times more "
"damage. Sneak Attacks with Bows, one-handed weapons and bare hands deal 2 "
"times more damage.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</>'s Sneak Attacks with a Dagger deal 8 times "
"more damage. Sneak Attacks with Bows, one-handed weapons and bare hands deal "
"3 times more damage.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> makes less noise while moving and wearing "
"boots, making them harder to detect.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> is harder to detect in bright environments.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</>'s Sneak Attacks ignore their opponent's "
"armor.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Sneak, <RT_BlueMed>move around "
"undetected</> or successfully <RT_BlueMed>pick pockets</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"LightArmor\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• LIGHT ARMOR •</>\n"
"The Light Armor Skill affects your ability to use <RT_BlueMed>Light armors</> "
"more effectively.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</>'s Light armor degrades 50% faster.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</>'s Light Armor degrades at a normal rate.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</>'s Light Armor degrades 50% slower.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</>'s equipped Light Armor does not encumber them at "
"all.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> gains a 50% increase in protection when exclusively "
"wearing Light Armor.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Light Armor, <RT_BlueMed>get hit</> "
"while wearing Light Armor gear.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Acrobatics\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• ACROBATICS •</>\n"
"The Acrobatics Skill affects your <RT_BlueMed>ability to jump higher</> and "
"<RT_BlueMed>avoid damage when falling</> from high heights.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> has no particular perk.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> can Dodge by pressing <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Block\"/> + <IA id=\"IA_Game_Movement_Jump\"/> while "
"moving.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> consumes 50% less Fatigue when jumping.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can jump over the surface of water.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> consumes 75% less Fatigue when jumping and takes "
"50% less fall damage.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Acrobatics, <RT_BlueMed>jump</> or "
"<RT_BlueMed>take damage from falling</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Security\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• SECURITY •</>\n"
"The Security Skill affects your ability to use lockpicks to <RT_BlueMed>open "
"locked doors and containers</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> makes up to four tumblers fall when they fail and "
"break a pick.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> makes up to three tumblers fall when they fail "
"and break a pick.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> makes up to two tumblers fall when they fail "
"and break a pick.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> makes only one tumbler fall when they fail and "
"break a pick.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> makes no tumblers fall when they fail and break a "
"pick.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Security, <RT_BlueMed>set "
"tumblers</> while lockpicking.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Mercantile\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• MERCANTILE •</>\n"
"The Mercantile Skill affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>get better deals</> "
"when buying or selling goods.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> sells items at a reduced price when they are in bad "
"condition.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> always sells items as if they were in perfect "
"condition. They are offered better items.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> can buy and sell any item to any vendor, even "
"if they usually do not barter that type of wares. Merchants offer them even "
"better items.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Expert</> can invest in a shop to permanently increase that "
"merchant's available gold by 500. Additionally, all shops in the world always "
"have 500 more gold available for barter.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Master</> buys and sells items at base cost. Merchants offer "
"them their best items.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Mercantile, gain Gold by "
"<RT_BlueMed>selling items</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Speechcraft\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• SPEECHCRAFT •</>\n"
"The Speechcraft Skill affects your ability to use speech to "
"<RT_BlueMed>persuade listeners to like and trust you</>.\n"
"\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Novice</> has no particular perk.\n"
"• An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> loses disposition 50% less rapidly when trying "
"to persuade a character.\n"
"• A <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman</> gains a free rotation of a wedge when trying to "
"persuade a character.\n"
"• For an <RT_BlueMed>Expert</>, bribes cost 50% less.\n"
"• For a <RT_BlueMed>Master</>, disposition doesn't decrease over time when "
"trying to persuade a character. Disposition is also less impacted by the most "
"disliked action.\n"
"\n"
"To <RT_BlueMed>increase your level</> in Speechcraft, increase or decrease "
"someone's Disposition through <RT_BlueMed>persuasion</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt ""
"ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_EnchantingWithSigilStones"
msgid ""
"As you venture into the <RT_BlueMed>Oblivion realms</>, you will gather "
"powerful daedric stones known as <RT_BlueMed>Sigil Stones</>.\n"
"Select them in your inventory to <RT_BlueMed>enchant any unenchanted "
"equipment</> without the need of an Altar of Enchanting.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"SigilStone\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"There are <RT_BlueMed>many different types</> of Sigil Stones, but all have a "
"pair of <RT_BlueMed>mutually exclusive enchantments</>:\n"
"• One that affects your <RT_BlueMed>opponents</> or their abilities, and can "
"only be applied on <RT_BlueMed>weapons</>.\n"
"• Another that acts directly on <RT_BlueMed>yourself</>, and can be applied "
"on <RT_BlueMed>armors, clothings and jewelry</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"SigilStoneMenu\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"You can name your newly enchanted item to truly make it unique.\n"
"\n"
"Once you <RT_BlueMed>complete the enchantment, the stone vanishes</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_LevelingUp"
msgid ""
"As your Skills improve, you gain Experience.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>The higher the Skill level, the more Experience you "
"gain.</>\n"
"\n"
"When a Skill is improved, the <RT_BlueMed>level up bar</> appears, showing "
"the amount of Experience that was gained:\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"SkillUpWidget\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"When the <RT_BlueMed>bar is filled</>, you have gained enough Experience to "
"level up.\n"
"You can <RT_BlueMed>check</> at any time if you are <RT_BlueMed>ready to "
"level up</> by looking for <RT_BlueMed>this icon</> on the top right of the "
"screen:\n"
"<img id=\"LevelUpIcon\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"You can then <RT_BlueMed>level up</> by <RT_BlueMed>sleeping in a "
"bed</>.\n"
"\n"
"You can level up <RT_BlueMed>several times in a row</> if you have not slept "
"for a while and have improved your Skills enough for multiple levels."
msgstr ""

