msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Enchanting"
msgid ""
"By joining an object with the essence of a creature captured inside a "
"<RT_BlueMed>Soul Gem</>, you can infuse your equipment with "
"<RT_BlueMed>powerful magic</>.\n"
"\n"
"This process requires the use of an <RT_BlueMed>Altar of Enchanting</>, "
"usually found at the <RT_BlueMed>Arcane University</>.\n"
"Provided they are not already enchanted, any item that can be worn and any "
"weapon that can be wielded can be enchanted.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"EnchantAltar\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"You must <RT_BlueMed>provide the items</> that are to be enchanted, the "
"<RT_BlueMed>filled Soul Gems</>, and the <RT_BlueMed>gold</> "
"required.\n"
"Select first <RT_BlueMed>item to enchant</>, then a <RT_BlueMed>filled Soul "
"Gem</>. After selecting both, you will be able to <RT_BlueMed>choose the "
"magic effects</> you would like to apply.\n"
"\n"
"You can give your newly enchanted item a name to make it more special to "
"you.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Enchanted weapons and staves</> can only be used a limited number "
"of times before needing to be <RT_BlueMed>recharged</> with filled soul "
"gems.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Enchanted armor and clothing</>, on the other hand, are passive "
"effects, and <RT_BlueMed>never require recharging</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"EnchantedWeaponBar\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>"
msgstr ""

