msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Attributes"
msgid ""
"Each character's traits and capabilities are defined by their "
"<RT_BlueMed>eight primary Attributes</>.\n"
"These usually range from 0 to 100, but can be pushed above 100 with "
"enchantments or other positive effects.\n"
"Attributes <RT_BlueMed>can be altered</> by magic, potions, enchanted items "
"or diseases.\n"
"\n"
"Raising your level allows you to increase your Attributes.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Strength\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• STRENGTH •</>\n"
"Strength affects the amount of <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with "
"<RT_BlueMed>Longswords, Claymores, Maces, War Axes, Battle-Axes, "
"Warhammers</>, and your <RT_BlueMed>bare hands</>.\n"
"Each point in Strength also increases your <RT_BlueMed>maximum "
"Encumberance</> by 5, allowing you to carry more items and "
"equipment.\n"
"Strength also has an effect on your <RT_BlueMed>maximum Health</>, though is "
"not as impactful as Endurance in that regard.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Intelligence\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• INTELLIGENCE •</>\n"
"Intelligence determines your <RT_BlueMed>maximum "
"Magicka</>.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>High Intelligence</> may be necessary to have enough Magicka to "
"cast the <RT_BlueMed>most powerful spells</>.\n"
"Increasing Intelligence <RT_BlueMed>does not</> increase the rate at which "
"you regenerate Magicka.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Willpower\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• WILLPOWER •</>\n"
"Willpower determines how quickly you <RT_BlueMed>regenerate Magicka</>, both "
"in and out of combat.\n"
"Increasing Willpower also greatly increases your <RT_BlueMed>maximum "
"Fatigue</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Agility\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• AGILITY •</>\n"
"Agility affects the amount of <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with "
"<RT_BlueMed>Daggers, Shortswords and Bows</>.\n"
"It also increases your <RT_BlueMed>maximum Fatigue</>, though is not as "
"impactful as Willpower in that regard.\n"
"Agility also defines how quickly you <RT_BlueMed>regenerate Fatigue</>, both "
"in and out of combat.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Speed\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• SPEED •</>\n"
"Speed determines how <RT_BlueMed>fast</> you walk, swim, run and sprint.\n"
"A <RT_BlueMed>high Speed</> can allow you to <RT_BlueMed>outrun most "
"enemies</>, and can be useful to move out of the way of melee and ranged "
"attacks.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Endurance\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• ENDURANCE •</>\n"
"Endurance greatly increases your <RT_BlueMed>maximum Health</>.\n"
"It also determines how much your Health will <RT_BlueMed>increase when you "
"raise levels</>. This increase is retroactive, making Endurance very "
"worthwile at higher levels.\n"
"Endurance also defines how quickly you <RT_BlueMed>regenerate Health</> out "
"of combat.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Personality\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• PERSONALITY •</>\n"
"Personality affects <RT_BlueMed>how much people like you</>, allowing you to "
"<RT_BlueMed>obtain meaningful information</> from people more "
"easily.\n"
"Increasing Personality allows you to <RT_BlueMed>negociate better deals</> "
"with merchants, and allows you to <RT_BlueMed>avoid combat</> more often as "
"fewer enemies will attack you and more people will accept yields.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Luck\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• LUCK •</>\n"
"Luck secretly increases or decreases the final level of <RT_BlueMed>all your "
"skills</>, having an effect on everything you do.\n"
"Luck <RT_BlueMed>above 50</> influences events in <RT_BlueMed>your favor</> "
"while Luck <RT_BlueMed>below 50</> influences events <RT_BlueMed>against "
"you</>."
msgstr ""

