msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Guilds"
msgid ""
"Guilds are organizations that <RT_BlueMed>you can join</> during your "
"journey. Most factions have Guild Halls scattered around Cyrodiil. There are "
"<RT_BlueMed>five major Guilds</>:\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Faction_FightersGuild\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• THE FIGHTERS GUILD •</>\n"
"The Fighters Guild is a faction dedicated to providing <RT_BlueMed>mercenary "
"services</>, including combat-related tasks such as <RT_BlueMed>protecting "
"townsfolk, slaying creatures and clearing dungeons</>.\n"
"\n"
"To join the Fighters Guild, seek out <RT_BlueMed>Azzan</> in Anvil, "
"<RT_BlueMed>Bruz gro-Khash</> in Cheydinhal or <RT_BlueMed>Vilena Donton</> "
"in Chorrol.\n"
"\n"
"Once a member of the guild, you gain access to the guild’s resources, "
"including its <RT_BlueMed>network of trainers</> and the opportunity to "
"undertake contracts for <RT_BlueMed>gold and gear</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Faction_MagesGuild\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• THE MAGES GUILD •</>\n"
"The Mages Guild is a scholarly and magical organization dedicated to the "
"<RT_BlueMed>study and practice of magic</>. It serves as a central "
"institution for mages across Tamriel, providing education, resources, and "
"research opportunities in various schools of magic.\n"
"\n"
"To join the Mages Guild, seek out <RT_BlueMed>any of the seven guild hall "
"leaders</>. If you do not know who the leaders are, try asking any Mages "
"Guild member.\n"
"\n"
"Once a member of the guild, you gain access to the guild's resources and can "
"train in various schools of magic.\n"
"Once you've obtained all the Mages Guild Recommendations, you are permitted "
"into the Arcane University, allowing you to enchant gear and create your own "
"spells.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Faction_ThievesGuild\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• THE THIEVES GUILD •</>\n"
"The Thieves Guild is a clandestine and highly organized network of criminals "
"specializing in <RT_BlueMed>theft, burglary, and other illicit "
"activities</>.\n"
"\n"
"To join the Thieves Guild, try getting <RT_BlueMed>entangled with the law</> "
"in a way that attracts attention, or try locating the <RT_BlueMed>mysterious "
"Gray Fox</>.\n"
"\n"
"Once a member of the guild, you'll gain access to a variety of lucrative "
"<RT_BlueMed>theft-related jobs</>. You can also <RT_BlueMed>sell your stolen "
"goods</> to any of the guild's fences.\n"
"Doyens always keep a stock of <RT_BlueMed>Lockpicks</> available for "
"purchase, and offer you to pay off <RT_BlueMed>half of your active bounty to "
"clear your name</>, without losing your stolen items in the process.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Faction_DarkBrotherhood\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• THE DARK BROTHERHOOD •</>\n"
"The Dark Brotherhood is a <RT_BlueMed>secretive and deadly cult</> dedicated "
"to the worship of Sithis, the personification of chaos and change.\n"
"\n"
"To join the Dark Brotherhood, you must <RT_BlueMed>commit the ultimate "
"crime</>, and must know that the Dark Brotherhood recruits new members by "
"contacting them in their sleep.\n"
"\n"
"Once a member of the guild, you gain access to a sanctuary only available to "
"members, where you can <RT_BlueMed>purchase powerful magical items and "
"spells</>. You also gain access to <RT_BlueMed>Poisoned Apples</>.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Faction_Arena\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• THE ARENA •</>\n"
"The Arena in Oblivion is a combat organization where fighters "
"<RT_BlueMed>battle to the death for fame, glory and gold</> in front of a "
"roaring crowd.\n"
"\n"
"To join the Arena, visit the Arena District in the Imperial City and speak to "
"<RT_BlueMed>Owyn</>, the Blademaster in the Bloodworks.\n"
"\n"
"Once a member of the Arena, you can engage in a series of progressively "
"tougher battles, each offering significant <RT_BlueMed>gold rewards</> and a "
"chance to increase your <RT_BlueMed>Fame</>.\n"
"Victories also grant you access to <RT_BlueMed>better gear and equipment</>, "
"which can be used both in and outside the Arena."
msgstr ""

