msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Trespassing"
msgid ""
"If the crosshair turns red as you approach a door, you are about to trespass, "
"putting you on the wrong side of the law.\n"
"\n"
"When trespassing, the compass turns red to indicate that you should probably "
"leave before getting into trouble.\n"
"\n"
"In <RT_BlueMed>private areas</>, such as houses, <RT_BlueMed>you have about "
"30 seconds</> to conclude your business and leave. After that, you’ll be "
"warned by the owner that you’ve strayed beyond the velvet rope.\n"
"\n"
"In <RT_BlueMed>off-limits areas</>, such as the royal quarters in Castle "
"Anvil, an alarm will go out <RT_BlueMed>as soon as you are detected</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Yielding "
msgid ""
"If you get into a fight with an ally, you can put an end to the combat by "
"yielding to him. To yield, <RT_BlueMed>hold</> <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Block\"/> <RT_BlueMed>to block and interact</> with the "
"attacker. <RT_BlueMed>This will only work if their disposition is high "
"enough</> towards you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Yielding"
msgid ""
"If you get into a fight, you can try to <RT_BlueMed>peacefully put an end to "
"the combat</> by yielding. \n"
"\n"
"To yield, <RT_BlueMed>hold</> <IA id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Block\"/> to block, "
"then <RT_BlueMed>interact</> with the attacker.\n"
"Enemies may refuse to yield if their disposition towards you is too low. "
"Creatures never yield."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_SchoolOfIllusion"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic is the art of <RT_BlueMed>altering the senses and the mind of "
"entities</>.\n"
"\n"
"Wishing to trick a merchant, conceal your presence or immobilize enemies? "
"Mages specialized in Illusion, usually found at <RT_BlueMed>Bravil's Mages "
"Guild</>, can teach you how to cast such spells.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Charm\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• CHARM •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Temporarily increases target’s Disposition towards the caster.</> "
"When the effect ends, the target’s Disposition returns to its original "
"value.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Command\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• COMMAND •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Makes targeted creature or humanoid fight alongside the "
"caster.</> The magnitude defines the maximum level of the creature or "
"humanoid that can be affected.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Invisibility\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• INVISIBILITY •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Completely conceals the target from others.</> The effect ends if "
"the subject attacks, speaks, or interacts with items or doors. While others "
"cannot see the subject, they may still be able to hear them.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Chameleon\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• CHAMELEON •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Lets the target partially blend into their surroundings.</> The "
"magnitude defines the degree of invisibility, with 100% being equivalent to "
"the Invisibility effect. Unlike Invisibility, the effect doesn't end if the "
"subject attacks or interacts with objects. While others cannot fully see the "
"subject, they may still hear them.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"LightEye\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• LIGHT •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Illuminates the area around the target.</> The magnitude of the "
"effect defines the radius of the illuminated area.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"NightEye\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• NIGHT-EYE •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Grants the target the ability to see in the dark.</>\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Paralyze\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• PARALYZE •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Makes the target unable to move and attack.</>\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Silence\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• SILENCE •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Makes the target unable to cast spells.</>\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Calm\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• CALM •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Decreases the target's inclination to attack and prevents it from "
"moving and attacking.</> The effect ends if the subject takes damage. The "
"magnitude defines both the maximum level of the creature or humanoid that can "
"be affected and the amount by which the Aggression is decreased.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Frenzy\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• FRENZY •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Increases the target's inclination to attack.</> The magnitude "
"defines both the maximum level of the character that can be affected and the "
"amount by which the Aggression is increased. Creatures are "
"unaffected.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Demoralize\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• DEMORALIZE •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Decreases the target's willingness to fight.</> The magnitude "
"defines both the maximum level of the creature or humanoid that can be "
"affected and the amount by which the Confidence is decreased. Undead are "
"unaffected.\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"Rally\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• RALLY •</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Increases the target's willingness to fight.</> The magnitude is "
"the amount by which the Confidence is increased."
msgstr ""

