msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Alchemy"
msgid ""
"Provided you have a <RT_BlueMed>Mortar and Pestle</> on you, using any "
"alchemical apparatus from your inventory allows you to create "
"potions.\n"
"\n"
"Potions and poisons are made by <RT_BlueMed>combining two or more ingredients "
"that share the same effect</>. The \"Filters\" button can be handy if you are "
"looking for a specific effect.\n"
"\n"
"To add an ingredient, place it in one of the slots by <RT_BlueMed>pressing</> "
"<IA id=\"IA_UI_Generic_Accept\"/>.\n"
"You can add up to four ingredients, and <RT_BlueMed>all matching effects will "
"appear in the effect list</>, below the potion slots.\n"
"\n"
"Ingredient effects may be <RT_BlueMed>beneficial</> or "
"<RT_BlueMed>harmful.</>\n"
"A potion with <RT_BlueMed>only harmful effects</> is considered <RT_BlueMed>a "
"poison</>.\n"
"\n"
"You can name your creation to find it more easily in your inventory later "
"on.\n"
"\n"
"To consume a potion or apply a poison, select it in your Inventory and "
"<RT_BlueMed>press</> <IA id=\"IA_UI_Generic_Accept\"/>. You will be prompted "
"to confirm applying poisons to your equipped "
"weapon.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Apparatuses</>, such as <RT_BlueMed>Retorts, Calcinators and "
"Alembics</>, can greatly <RT_BlueMed>improve the potency</> of the potions "
"and poisons you create by increasing the magnitude and the duration of its "
"effects."
msgstr ""

