msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_MarklessLocations"
msgid ""
"Some landmarks in Cyrodiil do <RT_BlueMed>not appear on your map</> or your "
"compass, yet still offer noteworthy <RT_BlueMed>boons</>:\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• BIRTHSIGN STONES •</>\n"
"Birthsign Stones grant you a <RT_BlueMed>greater power</> linked to a "
"constellation. You can only have <RT_BlueMed>one of these powers at a "
"time</>, but it doesn't have to be the same as your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Birthsign</>.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• HEAVEN STONES •</>\n"
"Heaven Stones grant you a <RT_BlueMed>permanent greater power</>. Unlike "
"Birthsign Stones, you can have all greater powers "
"<RT_BlueMed>simultaneously</>.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• RUNE STONES •</>\n"
"Rune Stones summon one <RT_BlueMed>bound weapon</> and one <RT_BlueMed>bound "
"armor</> for 2 to 5 minutes. Each Rune Stone can only be used "
"<RT_BlueMed>once a day</>. There are three different Rune Stones, each giving "
"different weapon and armor types.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• AYLEID WELLS •</>\n"
"Ayleid Wells increase your total <RT_BlueMed>Magicka</> and your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Magicka regeneration</> for 5 minutes. They can only be used "
"<RT_BlueMed>once a day</>.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• WAYSHRINES •</>\n"
"Wayshrines cure most <RT_BlueMed>diseases</>, restore your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Health</> as well as your <RT_BlueMed>Attributes</>, and "
"<RT_BlueMed>increase one or more Attribute</> for 10 minutes.\n"
"Each wayshrine is dedicated to one of the Nine Divines. You cannot benefit "
"from their boons if you have <RT_BlueMed>Infamy</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Trainers"
msgid ""
"Some people, known as trainers, can be paid to train you in a specific "
"Skill.\n"
"\n"
"Many of these trainers are affiliated with guilds. Fighters Guild trainers "
"require guild membership, but Mages Guild and Thieves Guild trainers "
"don't.\n"
"\n"
"You can only train five times per level. Once you've reached your limit, you "
"will need to level up.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Basic trainers</> are skilled enough to train your Skills "
"<RT_BlueMed>up to 40</>.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Advanced trainers</> can train your Skills <RT_BlueMed>up to "
"70</>.\n"
"Only <RT_BlueMed>Master trainers</> can train your Skills <RT_BlueMed>above "
"70</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_PurchasingSpells"
msgid ""
"Some specialized merchants offer a variety of spells to purchase. When in "
"dialogue with them, select the <RT_BlueMed>spell purchase icon</> to ask that "
"person what spells they are selling.\n"
"<img id=\"Dialog_SpellTrade\" height=\"desired\" "
"width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"Purchasing spells is essential to <RT_BlueMed>be versatile</> and "
"<RT_BlueMed>keep up with the increasingly more dangerous world</>. It also "
"enables you to craft your own spells of that type at an Altar of Spellmaking."
msgstr ""

