msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryDescription_Notifications"
msgid ""
"When an event occurs, a notification appears on the top left on the screen "
"showing a summary of what transpired.\n"
"Learn more about the notification center."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Pickpocketing"
msgid ""
"When approaching someone from behind while <RT_BlueMed>sneaking</>, the "
"crosshair turns into a <RT_BlueMed>red hand icon</>.\n"
"Interacting with that character then allows you to pick their pockets, "
"showing you the victim's <RT_BlueMed>unequipped possessions</> that can be "
"pickpocketed.\n"
"\n"
"Each time you try to steal an item, <RT_BlueMed>your attempt can be "
"detected</>. The target's Sneak skill level and the value and amount of items "
"taken influences the success rate.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Even if you change your mind</> and don't steal anything, your "
"attempt can be detected.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>If detected</>, the victim's Disposition towards you will "
"decrease and they can possibly <RT_BlueMed>report your crime or attack "
"you</>. They will also remain vigilant, preventing you from picking their "
"pockets for a while."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Bartering"
msgid ""
"When bartering, both your inventory and the inventory of the person you are "
"bartering with are displayed side by side. You can <RT_BlueMed>switch between "
"both inventories</> to <RT_BlueMed>sell or buy items</>.\n"
"\n"
"Select any item you want to buy from the person and, <RT_BlueMed>provided you "
"have enough money</>, the item will be placed in your inventory.\n"
"\n"
"You can also sell items by selecting them from your inventory. However, "
"merchants have a <RT_BlueMed>limited amount of Gold</> they are willing to "
"pay on a <RT_BlueMed>single transaction</>.\n"
"\n"
"Additionally, the person you are bartering with may choose to accept or "
"reject any offer based on <RT_BlueMed>how much you are haggling</>. If the "
"offer is rejected, their Disposition will drop slightly."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Clairvoyance"
msgid ""
"When cast, the Clairvoyance spell creates a a blue light that will "
"<RT_BlueMed>guide you to your current objective</>.\n"
"\n"
"While your compass' quest marker shows you the straight-line direction to "
"your current objective, Clairvoyance shows you the path, <RT_BlueMed>taking "
"into account the twists and turns</>.\n"
"\n"
"This can be very useful if you become lost in a tortuous cave or ruin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt ""
"ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Settings_SettingDescription_ItemRotationInputType"
msgid ""
"When on hold, the item preview rotation mode is triggered by an hold input. "
"When on toggle, it is triggered with a single press and the item rotates by "
"itself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_TargetHealth&Name"
msgid ""
"When pointing your crosshair at a target, their health bar and name appear "
"under the compass at the center of the screen.\n"
"When looking at a boss, the health bar and name are shaped differently to "
"indicate the greater threat these enemies represent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Persuasion"
msgid ""
"When talking to most people, you can try to <RT_BlueMed>persuade</> them to "
"<RT_BlueMed>increase their Disposition</> towards you. This might incline "
"them to share <RT_BlueMed>more information</> or <RT_BlueMed>better trade "
"offers</>.\n"
"\n"
"When speaking to someone, press the <RT_BlueMed>Persuasion icon</> at the "
"bottom to start persuading them:\n"
"<img id=\"Dialog_Persuasion\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"At the center of the circle is displayed that character's Disposition towards "
"you, represented as a number between 0 and 100.\n"
"Their <RT_BlueMed>initial Disposition</> is based on a variety of factors, "
"including your <RT_BlueMed>Personality, race, reputation, faction "
"affiliations</> or how this person may feel about your <RT_BlueMed>previous "
"actions</>.\n"
"\n"
"From here, there are two ways to increase someone's disposition: persuading "
"them or bribing them.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• PERSUADING •</>\n"
"For each attempt at Persuasion, you must <RT_BlueMed>Admire, Boast, Joke, and "
"Coerce</>.\n"
"\n"
"You can only choose <RT_BlueMed>each action once</>, but in any order you "
"want. The Persuasion attempt will end only once <RT_BlueMed>all four "
"actions</> have been selected. \n"
"\n"
"These actions <RT_BlueMed>raise or lower</> the target‘s Disposition towards "
"you, depending on their <RT_BlueMed>temperament</>: each people always "
"<RT_BlueMed>love</> an action, <RT_BlueMed>like</> one, "
"<RT_BlueMed>dislike</> one and <RT_BlueMed>hate</> one.\n"
"You can predict how they will react to an action by <RT_BlueMed>looking at "
"their face</> while hovering that action.\n"
"\n"
"Each of the <RT_BlueMed>four quadrants</> is filled with one to four "
"<RT_BlueMed>wedges</>. The more wedges there are, the more "
"<RT_BlueMed>impactful</> the selected action will be.\n"
"Every time you select an action, all wedges rotate <RT_BlueMed>clockwise</>. "
"\n"
"\n"
"Try selecting <RT_BlueMed>larger wedges</> when they are aligned with actions "
"the person <RT_BlueMed>loves or likes</> to maximize the increase in "
"Disposition.\n"
"Try selecting <RT_BlueMed>smaller wedges</> when they are aligned with "
"actions they <RT_BlueMed>dislike or hate</>, to minimize the decrease in "
"Disposition.\n"
"\n"
"Their <RT_BlueMed>Disposition slowly decrease over time</>, so don't take too "
"long to choose your action.\n"
"\n"
"An <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice</> in <RT_BlueMed>Speechcraft</> can "
"<RT_BlueMed>rotate the wedges</> without selecting any action "
"<RT_BlueMed>once per Persuasion attempt</>.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>• BRIBING •</>\n"
"If persuading is not your kind, you can always try to <RT_BlueMed>Bribe</> "
"them instead.\n"
"If they <RT_BlueMed>accept your money</>, their Disposition towards you will "
"increase. Bribing can be <RT_BlueMed>quite expensive</> until your are an "
"Expert in Speechcraft. So should probably not rely on it too much."
msgstr ""

