msgctxt ""
"ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_CharacterSkillPerks_Description_LightArmorMaster"
msgid ""
"When wearing <RT_BlueMed>exclusively Light Armor</>, your protection is "
"<RT_BlueMed>greatly increased</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_IncreasingYourAttributes"
msgid ""
"When you <RT_BlueMed>level up</>, you are given the opportunity to distribute "
"virtues to <RT_BlueMed>increase your Attributes</>:\n"
"\n"
"<img id=\"LevelUpMenu\" height=\"desired\" width=\"desired\"/>\n"
"\n"
"You can assign <RT_BlueMed>up to five</> virtues into any Attribute. "
"<RT_BlueMed>Each virtue assigned</> to an Attribute <RT_BlueMed>increases it "
"by one</>.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Luck is an exception</>, as it requires <RT_BlueMed>four "
"virtues</> to increase by a <RT_BlueMed>single point</>.\n"
"\n"
"It is up to you how to distribute the virtues, but you may only increase "
"<RT_BlueMed>three Attributes</> per level up."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Sneaking"
msgid ""
"When you are sneaking, enemies have a <RT_BlueMed>harder time detecting "
"you</>.\n"
"You can use this to your advantage to <RT_BlueMed>pass by enemies</>, "
"<RT_BlueMed>pick their pockets</> or perform deadly <RT_BlueMed>Sneak "
"Attacks</>.\n"
"\n"
"To increase your chance of remaining undetected, <RT_BlueMed>avoid walking in "
"front of enemies</>, and <RT_BlueMed>prefer shadows</> over bright "
"areas.\n"
"Avoid noisy actions such as <RT_BlueMed>running</>, <RT_BlueMed>picking "
"locks</>, <RT_BlueMed>wearing heavy boots</> and <RT_BlueMed>interacting with "
"items</> when enemies are close by.\n"
"\n"
"The amount of damage you deal when performing <RT_BlueMed>Sneak Attacks</> "
"depends on the <RT_BlueMed>kind of weapon</> you use. \n"
"\n"
"While <RT_BlueMed>Daggers</> have the <RT_BlueMed>biggest damage bonus</>, "
"one-handed weapons, Bows and bare hands still have a decent damage "
"bonus.\n"
"Two-handed weapons <RT_BlueMed>do not get any damage bonus</> for performing "
"Sneak Attacks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_Jail"
msgid ""
"When<RT_BlueMed> arrested</>, you may decide to surrender and go to "
"<RT_BlueMed>jail</>. If you do, you are escorted to a cell in the nearest "
"castle or prison. <RT_BlueMed>Your possessions are seized</>, although you "
"may manage to hide a Lockpick.\n"
"\n"
"You can <RT_BlueMed>serve out your sentence</> by sleeping on the bed "
"<RT_BlueMed>or escape by picking the lock</> and sneaking out.\n"
"\n"
"If you decide to <RT_BlueMed>serve your sentence</>, some of your Skills will "
"be <RT_BlueMed>permanently lowered</>. The amount of Skills decreases depends "
"on the total bounty you had when arrested.\n"
"Your debt will be considered paid, and you will receive all your items back, "
"except for stolen items.\n"
"\n"
"If you decide to <RT_BlueMed>escape</> and manage to pick the cell's lock, "
"anyone in the prison will attack you on sight.\n"
"If you successfully leave the prison, you can try to get your items back. "
"They are usually placed in a locked Evidence Chest, near the exit.\n"
"In any case, you will gain an <RT_BlueMed>additional bounty</> on your head "
"for your jailbreak."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_MeleeAttacks"
msgid ""
"Whether you fight bare-handed or with a Claymore, you can perform "
"<RT_BlueMed>two kinds of attacks</>.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Regular Attacks</> are performed by pressing <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Attack\"/>. \n"
"They consume a <RT_BlueMed>small</> amount of <RT_BlueMed>Fatigue</> and can "
"be chained together. Swinging heavier weapons consumes more "
"Fatigue.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> are performed by holding <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Attack\"/>. \n"
"They deal <RT_BlueMed>significantly more damage</> but also consume "
"<RT_BlueMed>more Fatigue</> and can leave you open to counter-attacks.\n"
"You can <RT_BlueMed>Power Attack in different directions</> to reposition "
"yourself during combat."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_AltarDynamicTexts/LOC_AD_Help_EntryContent_MeleeAttacks "
msgid ""
"Whether you fight bare-handed or with a mighty claymore, there are two ways "
"to fight:\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>NORMAL ATTACKS</>\n"
"Press </> <IA id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Attack\"/> <RT_BlueMed> to perform a Normal "
"Attack</>. Press again quickly to chain Normal Attacks and deliver "
"consecutive blows. Each attack consumes a small portion of your Fatigue. Be "
"careful not to exhaust your energy.\n"
"\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>POWER ATTACKS</>\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>To perform a Power Attack</>, hold</> <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Attack\"/>. Power attacks can deal significant damage, "
"but they also consume more Fatigue and can leave you open to counter-"
"attacks.\n"
"<RT_BlueMed>The direction you are moving while performing a Power Attack "
"determines the resulting action.</>"
msgstr ""

