msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity05"
msgid ""
"...But should the Dragonfires fail, and should no heir of our joined blood "
"wear the Amulet of Kings, then shall the Empire descend into darkness..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Charactergen02"
msgid ""
"...So long as you and your descendants shall wear the Amulet of Kings, then "
"shall this Dragonfire burn -- an eternal flame -- as a sign to all men and "
"gods of our faithfulness..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity04"
msgid ""
"...So long as you and your descendants shall wear the Amulet of Kings, then "
"shall this Dragonfire burn -- an eternal flame -- as a sign to all men and "
"gods of our faithfulness..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Agent"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Charming</> when they can be seen, and <RT_BlueMed>nearly "
"invisible</> when lurking in the shadows."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Barbarian"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Fearsome brutes</> who inspire fear and dread in the hearts of "
"their enemies. Like a storm, <RT_BlueMed>swift and powerful</>. Finding "
"little use for heavy armor, they rely on smashing their foes into the ground."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Pilgrim"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Hearty</> folk, well-versed in the tomes of old. They profit in "
"life by <RT_BlueMed>bartering</> in the market, or by "
"<RT_BlueMed>persuading</> the weak-minded."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Bard"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Intelligent and personable</>, they prefer to accomplish tasks "
"with their words first, and sword second."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Assassin"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Nimble and quiet</>, they move in darkness to strike at the "
"unsuspecting. Locks hold no doors shut for them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Monk"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Quick and cunning</> with the <RT_BlueMed>empty hand</>, they are "
"<RT_BlueMed>strong in spirit</>. They prefer to solve conflict by arrow or by "
"fist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Nightblade"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Spell and shadow</> are their friends. By darkness they move with "
"haste, <RT_BlueMed>casting magic</> to benefit their circumstances."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Witchhunter"
msgid ""
"<RT_BlueMed>Swift on foot</>, and <RT_BlueMed>clever with spells</>, they use "
"<RT_BlueMed>distance</> as their ally. Slower adversaries are fodder for "
"their arrows."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksAcrobatics03"
msgid "A Journeyman of Acrobatics uses less Fatigue when jumping."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksArmorer03"
msgid "A Journeyman of Armorer can use repair hammers twice as long."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat09"
msgid ""
"A Journeyman of Blade's Power Attacks weaken their opponents to normal weapon "
"attacks for a brief duration."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksBlock02"
msgid "A Journeyman of Block loses slightly less Fatigue when blocking a hit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat08"
msgid "A Journeyman of Blunt's Power Attacks grant them a temporary shield."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat10"
msgid ""
"A Journeyman of Hand-to-Hand can damage creatures that are immune to normal "
"weapons."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat07"
msgid ""
"A Journeyman of Hand-to-Hand's Power Attacks have a chance to disarm their "
"opponent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksHeavy03"
msgid "A Journeyman of Heavy Armor has it degrade more slowly."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksLight03"
msgid "A Journeyman of Light Armor has it degrade more slowly."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMarksman03"
msgid ""
"A Journeyman of Marksman can focus their vision by holding Block while "
"shooting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMercantile02"
msgid ""
"A Journeyman of Mercantile can buy and sell any item with someone who barters."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksSneak03"
msgid "A Journeyman of Sneak moves much more quietly."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksAcrobatics04"
msgid ""
"A Master of Acrobatics takes very few damage from their fall and uses almost "
"no fatigue when jumping."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksArmorer04"
msgid "A Master of Armorer can repair items without using up his hammers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat02"
msgid ""
"A Master of Blade's Power Attacks make their opponents even more vulnerable "
"to normal weapon attacks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksBlock04"
msgid "A Master of Block loses almost no Fatigue when blocking."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat03"
msgid "A Master of Blunt's Power Attacks grant them even more shield."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat04"
msgid ""
"A Master of Hand-to-Hand's Regular Attacks reduce their opponents Fatigue a "
"lot faster."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksHeavy05"
msgid "A Master of Heavy Armor is not encumbered by wearing it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksLight04"
msgid ""
"A Master of Light Armor is much more protected when wearing exclusively Light "
"Armor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMarksman05"
msgid "A Master of Marksman has a good chance of paralyzing their target."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksSneak05"
msgid ""
"A Master of Sneak ignores an opponent's armor when attacking while sneaking."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksLight01"
msgid "A Novice of Light Armor has it degrade faster."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMarksman01"
msgid "A Novice of Marksman loses Fatigue when drawing a bow."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksSneak01"
msgid ""
"A Novice of Sneak deals extra damage when attacking while undetected, "
"particularly with Daggers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Crusader"
msgid ""
"A combatant who wields the power of <RT_BlueMed>brute strength</> and "
"<RT_BlueMed>medicinal knowledge</>. Cheating death after every fight, they "
"rely on their keen <RT_BlueMed>knowledge of restoration</> to fight yet again."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills03"
msgid "A high Willpower allows you to regenerate your Magicka faster."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Archer"
msgid ""
"A marksman, <RT_BlueMed>adept at combat at great distances</>. Able to take "
"down most foes before they have a chance to draw sword."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameAnvil02"
msgid ""
"A number of shabby abandoned houses mar the essential beauty of the town of "
"Anvil."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Battlemage"
msgid ""
"Able to resolve most conflicts with either spell or sword. They are a deadly "
"mix of <RT_BlueMed>scholar and soldier</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_FightersGuild03"
msgid ""
"According to the Fighters Guild charter, no private contracts may offend "
"against the laws and customs of the counties and the Imperium. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlock"
msgid ""
"Affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you <RT_BlueMed>mitigate</> when "
"blocking an attack."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlade"
msgid ""
"Affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with <RT_BlueMed>Blade</> "
"weapons."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlunt"
msgid ""
"Affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with <RT_BlueMed>Blunt</> "
"weapons."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMarksman"
msgid ""
"Affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with <RT_BlueMed>Bows</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHandToHand"
msgid ""
"Affects how much <RT_BlueMed>damage</> you deal with your <RT_BlueMed>bare "
"hands</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAthletics"
msgid "Affects how quickly you <RT_BlueMed>run, swim and sprint</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlchemy"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>create potions</> and <RT_BlueMed>obtain "
"greater benefits</> from alchemical ingredients."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMercantile"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>get better deals</> when buying or "
"selling goods."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAcrobatics"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>jump higher</> and <RT_BlueMed>withstand "
"falls</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillArmorer"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>maintain</> weapons and armor at "
"<RT_BlueMed>maximum efficiency</>. Broken weapons and armor are less "
"effective."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSneak"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>move unseen and unheard</> by observers, "
"and your odds of getting away with <RT_BlueMed>pickpocketing</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSpeechcraft"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>persuade listeners</> to like and trust "
"you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillConjuration"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to <RT_BlueMed>summon</> creatures, weapons and armor, "
"and <RT_BlueMed>turn the undead</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMysticism"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to cast spells to <RT_BlueMed>absorb magic, reflect "
"damage, dispel, move objects, sense life, reveal paths</> and "
"<RT_BlueMed>bind souls</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlteration"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to cast spells to <RT_BlueMed>breathe or walk on water, "
"open locks, reduce encumbrance</>, and <RT_BlueMed>shield yourself</> from "
"physical and magical damage."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillIllusion"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to cast spells to <RT_BlueMed>charm, conceal, create "
"light, silence, paralyze, command</> and <RT_BlueMed>affect aggressivity</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillDestruction"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to cast spells to <RT_BlueMed>inflict elemental "
"damage</> and <RT_BlueMed>weaken</> your opponents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillRestoration"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to cast spells to <RT_BlueMed>restore, fortify and "
"absorb attributes, cure diseases</>, and <RT_BlueMed>improve resistances</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHeavyArmor"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to use <RT_BlueMed>Heavy armors</> more effectively."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillLightArmor"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to use <RT_BlueMed>Light armors</> more effectively."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSecurity"
msgid ""
"Affects your ability to use lockpicks to <RT_BlueMed>open locked doors and "
"containers</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAcrobatics_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"After long, arduous hours of practicing jumping and controlling your falls, "
"you have become a Journeyman of Acrobatics. It now costs <RT_BlueMed>much "
"less Fatigue</> to jump."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAcrobatics_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"After long, arduous hours of practicing jumping and controlling your falls, "
"you have become a Master of Acrobatics. Your legs are harder than steel, "
"<RT_BlueMed>greatly reducing fall damage</>. It now <RT_BlueMed>costs even "
"less Fatigue</> to jump."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAcrobatics_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"After long, arduous hours of practicing jumping and controlling your falls, "
"you have become an Apprentice of Acrobatics. You are now able to "
"<RT_BlueMed>Dodge</> by pressing <IA id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Block\"/> + <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Movement_Jump\"/> <RT_BlueMed>while moving</>, allowing you to "
"<RT_BlueMed>quickly reposition yourself</> and avoid attacks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAcrobatics_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"After long, arduous hours of practicing jumping and controlling your falls, "
"you have become an Expert of Acrobatics. You are now able to jump on water. "
"With practice, you can jump several times in a row all the way across a body "
"of water."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills07"
msgid "Agility allows you to do more damage with Bows, Daggers and Shortswords."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_HighElf"
msgid ""
"Also known as \"Altmer\" in their homeland of Summerset Isle, the High Elves "
"are <RT_BlueMed>exceptionally gifted in the arcane arts</>, they also boast "
"<RT_BlueMed>resistance to illness</>. However, they are also somewhat "
"<RT_BlueMed>vulnerable to fire, frost and shock</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DarkElf"
msgid ""
"Also known as \"Dunmer\" in their homeland of Morrowind, the Dark Elves are "
"noted for their <RT_BlueMed>skilled and balanced integration of the sword, "
"the bow and destruction magic</>. They are <RT_BlueMed>resistant to fire</> "
"and can <RT_BlueMed>summon an ancestral ghost</> for aid."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsAlteration04"
msgid ""
"Alteration magic has a Shield spell that temporarily reduces the damage your "
"enemies do to you in combat."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsAlteration01"
msgid ""
"Alteration magic has spells that decrease the weight of the items you carry, "
"or increase the weight of the items your enemies carry."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsAlteration05"
msgid ""
"Alteration magic has spells that let you breathe underwater or walk on the "
"water's surface."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsAlteration02"
msgid ""
"Alteration magic has spells that shield you from fire, frost or lightning."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsAlteration03"
msgid "Alteration magic has spells that unlock doors and treasure chests."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault13"
msgid ""
"Amber is often found in root tunnels. It is rumored that a smith in New "
"Sheoth is able to fashion weapons and armor from Amber."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksAcrobatics02"
msgid "An Apprentice of Acrobatics can dodge quickly to a side."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksArmorer02"
msgid "An Apprentice of Armorer can repair magical weapons and armor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksBlock01"
msgid ""
"An Apprentice of Block does not have their shield or weapon damaged by "
"blocking."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksHeavy02"
msgid "An Apprentice of Heavy Armor has it degrade at a normal rate."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksLight02"
msgid "An Apprentice of Light Armor has it degrade normally."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMarksman02"
msgid "An Apprentice of Marksman no longer loses Fatigue when drawing a bow."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksArmorer05"
msgid ""
"An Expert in Armorer can repair items beyond 100%, improving their usefulness."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat06"
msgid ""
"An Expert of Blade's Regular Attacks have a chance to temporarily make their "
"opponents bleed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksBlock03"
msgid "An Expert of Block can perform a shield bash to stagger opponents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat05"
msgid ""
"An Expert of Blunt's Regular Attacks have a chance to temporarly silence "
"their opponents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksHeavy04"
msgid "An Expert of Heavy Armor is greatly less encumbered by it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksLight05"
msgid "An Expert of Light Armor is not encumbered while wearing it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMarksman04"
msgid "An Expert of Marksman has a slight chance of paralyzing their target."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMercantile03"
msgid "An Expert of Mercantile can invest their gold in stores."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksSneak04"
msgid "An Expert of Sneak is harder to detect, even in bright environments."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameKvatch01"
msgid ""
"Antus Pinder led a hopeless defense against a superior force. Despite a grave "
"defeat, his statue stands in Kvatch to honor his courage and spirit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameAnvil04"
msgid ""
"Anvil's Chapel of Dibella, the goddess of love, grants healing, curing, and "
"restoration of damaged attributes for those good pilgrims who pray at the "
"Altar of the Nine."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE08Load01"
msgid ""
"Areas conquered by the forces of Order are drained of energy, leaving them "
"dead and lifeless."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace09"
msgid ""
"Argonians can breathe underwater, are immune to poison, and resistant to "
"disease."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat08"
msgid "Arrows can be recovered from fallen creatures and characters."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillIllusion_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"As a new Apprentice of Illusion, you know what is and isn't real, and how to "
"fool the minds of your opponents. You can now cast <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice "
"level Illusion spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillIllusion_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"As a new Expert of Illusion, you know what is and isn't real, and how to fool "
"the minds of your opponents. You can now cast <RT_BlueMed>Expert level "
"Illusion spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillIllusion_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"As a new Journeyman of Illusion, you know what is and isn't real, and how to "
"fool the minds of your opponents. You can now cast <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman "
"level Illusion spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillIllusion_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"As a new Master of Illusion, you know what is and isn't real, and how to fool "
"the minds of your opponents. You can now cast <RT_BlueMed>all Illusion "
"spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDialogue01"
msgid "Asking about rumors may lead you to great treasure."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksAthletics03"
msgid "Asking people about rumours might hint you at important quests."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameChorrol04"
msgid ""
"At the Altar of the Nine in Chorrol's Chapel of Stendarr, pray and be healed, "
"cured, and restored in all your attributes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth09"
msgid ""
"Attempting to pick up objects makes you easier to detect. The heavier the "
"object, the more likely a nearby person will suddenly spot you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault04"
msgid ""
"Baliwogs are thought to be the larval form of Grummites, although this "
"relationship has never been proven."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SorcererTrainer"
msgid ""
"Besting the most well-equipped fighters, they rely on the spells of the "
"mystic arts.  Unique to these mages is the bodily stamina to be armed with "
"the thickest armor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Sorcerer"
msgid ""
"Besting the most well-equipped fighters, they rely on the spells of the "
"mystic arts. Unique to these <RT_BlueMed>mages</> is the <RT_BlueMed>bodily "
"stamina</> to be armed with the <RT_BlueMed>thickest armor</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MS05Dreamworld01"
msgid ""
"Beware, the death of the dreamer means the death of those who share his dream."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat09"
msgid "Blocking attacks causes your opponents to recoil briefly."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat07"
msgid ""
"Blocking damage works with either a shield, a weapon or your fists, but a "
"shield is more effective."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat11"
msgid ""
"Blocking reduces the damage you take based on your Block Skill level, at the "
"cost of Fatigue. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBravil03"
msgid ""
"Bravil's night air is damp and noisome because of the river channels that "
"serve as Bravil's sewers, and because of the nearby swamps where insects and "
"diseases breed in abundance."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE10Load01"
msgid ""
"Brellach is the stronghold of the Golden Saints. Few beyond the Saints are "
"ever permitted inside."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace03"
msgid ""
"Bretons have more Magicka, and higher resistance to it, than other races."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills13"
msgid ""
"Bribing someone is often the best way to get information, especially if your "
"skill in Speechcraft is low."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat02"
msgid "Broken armor pieces offer much less protection."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat01"
msgid "Broken weapons deal much less damage."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBruma03"
msgid ""
"Bruma builds in wood harvested from the native forests of the High Jeralls, "
"and her houses and halls often bear decorative carved timbers in the Nordic "
"style."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBruma02"
msgid ""
"Bruma's chilly winds and alpine climate favors dwellings built partly below "
"ground level to conserve heat."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault16"
msgid ""
"Buy a house so you always have a place to sleep. There are houses for sale in "
"each city."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameAnvil05"
msgid ""
"Chapel priests and healers sell spells from the College of Restoration. From "
"other colleges, they also offer a few select spells that benefit mankind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBravil05"
msgid ""
"Chapel priests and healers sell spells from the College of Restoration. From "
"other colleges, they also offer a few select spells that benefit mankind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBruma05"
msgid ""
"Chapel priests and healers sell spells from the College of Restoration. From "
"other colleges, they also offer a few select spells that benefit mankind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCheydinhal04"
msgid ""
"Chapel priests and healers sell spells from the College of Restoration. From "
"other colleges, they also offer a few select spells that benefit mankind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameChorrol05"
msgid ""
"Chapel priests and healers sell spells from the College of Restoration. From "
"other colleges, they also offer a few select spells that benefit mankind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameLeyawiin03"
msgid ""
"Chapel priests and healers sell spells from the College of Restoration. From "
"other colleges, they also offer a few select spells that benefit mankind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkingrad03"
msgid ""
"Chapel priests and healers sell spells from the College of Restoration. From "
"other colleges, they also offer a few select spells that benefit mankind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault10"
msgid ""
"Chorrol, Anvil, Kvatch, and Skingrad counties represent the heartland of "
"western Cyrodiil, a region known as Colovia."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Nord"
msgid ""
"Citizens of Skyrim, they are a tall and fair-haired people. "
"<RT_BlueMed>Strong and hardy</>, Nords are famous for their "
"<RT_BlueMed>resistance to cold</>. They are <RT_BlueMed>highly talented "
"warriors</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE08SoldierClass"
msgid "Class for the allies in SE08"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MS12PalePassRuins"
msgid ""
"Commander Mishaxhi, one of the Akaviri's greatest tacticians, commanded the "
"fort at Pale Pass."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsConjuration04"
msgid ""
"Conjuration magic has a Turn Undead spell that causes undead enemies to flee."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsConjuration02"
msgid ""
"Conjuration magic has spells that summon powerful daedric creatures to fight "
"for you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsConjuration01"
msgid ""
"Conjuration magic has spells that summon powerful magic armor or weapons."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsConjuration03"
msgid ""
"Conjuration magic has spells that summon powerful undead creatures to fight "
"for you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBravil01"
msgid ""
"Count Regulus Terentius, once a noted tournament champion, is widely "
"recognized by his people as a drunken wastrel and ne'er-do-well."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameChorrol02"
msgid ""
"Countess Arriana Valga is the Lady of Chorrol. However, her deceased husband, "
"Count Charus Valga, was the hereditary Count of Chorrol. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameAnvil01"
msgid ""
"Countess Millona Umbranox of Anvil is well-loved by her people. She lost her "
"husband many years ago."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBruma01"
msgid ""
"Countess Narina Carvain is a dutiful chapelgoer, and a respected ruler, "
"though she is a cunning and ruthless negotiator."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Chapels04"
msgid ""
"Criminals with bounties! Your prayers at the chapel for healing, curing, and "
"restoration may be denied for your sins! Clear the bounties from your head, "
"and seek forgiveness!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace06"
msgid ""
"Dark Elves are resistant to fire and also have the power of Ancestor "
"Guardian, which summons a spirit to fight for them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE10Load04"
msgid ""
"Dark Seducers cast into the waters of Oblivion return to the Shivering Isles "
"through Pinnacle Rock. The process is considered sacred and secret."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHeavyArmor_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Days and weeks of constant use make wearing heavy armor tolerable, but not "
"comfortable. You have learned to adapt to its weight and use it in combat. As "
"a Journeyman of Heavy Armor, <RT_BlueMed>your plate mail is now damaged at a "
"lower rate</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHeavyArmor_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Days and weeks of constant use make wearing heavy armor tolerable, but not "
"comfortable. You have learned to adapt to its weight and use it in combat. As "
"a Master of Heavy Armor, <RT_BlueMed>your plate mail no longer encumbers you "
"at all</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHeavyArmor_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Days and weeks of constant use make wearing heavy armor tolerable, but not "
"comfortable. You have learned to adapt to its weight and use it in combat. As "
"an Apprentice of Heavy Armor, <RT_BlueMed>your plate mail is now damaged at a "
"normal rate</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHeavyArmor_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Days and weeks of constant use make wearing heavy armor tolerable, but not "
"comfortable. You have learned to adapt to its weight and use it in combat. As "
"an Expert of Heavy Armor, <RT_BlueMed>your plate mail no longer encumbers you "
"as much</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SESettlement02"
msgid ""
"Deepwallow is a small Dementia community built on a swamp. The citizens are "
"not fond of strangers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksAcrobatics01"
msgid "Depleting an opponent's Fatigue using magical effects knocks them down."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat03"
msgid "Depleting an opponent's Fatigue using physical attacks staggers them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsDestruction01"
msgid ""
"Destruction magic has spells that directly damage Fatigue, Health, or Magicka."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsDestruction02"
msgid ""
"Destruction magic has spells that disintegrate weapons and armor, making them "
"break sooner."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsDestruction05"
msgid ""
"Destruction magic has spells that harness fire, frost or lightning to kill "
"your enemies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsDestruction04"
msgid ""
"Destruction magic has spells that temporarily drain Fatigue, Health or "
"Magicka."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsDestruction03"
msgid ""
"Destruction magic has spells that temporarily drain the Attributes or Skills "
"of your enemies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsDestruction06"
msgid ""
"Destruction magic has spells that weaken your enemy's resistance to disease, "
"fire, frost, lightning, magic, normal weapons or poison."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SancreTorLoad02"
msgid ""
"During the Sack of Sancre Tor, General Talos is said to have recovered the "
"Amulet of Kings from the tomb of Reman III. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace01"
msgid "Each race has its own set of special abilities and powers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault11"
msgid ""
"Eastern Cyrodiil is known as Nibenay. The peoples and styles of Bravil, "
"Leyawiin, and the Imperial City are defined by Nibenese culture."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault06"
msgid "Elytra are vicious insects that use deadly poisons to kill their prey."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault13"
msgid ""
"Enchanting and Spellmaking can only be performed by Mages Guild members at "
"the Arcane University."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills09"
msgid "Endurance greatly affects how much Health you have."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE04Load01"
msgid ""
"Felldew is a dangerous toxin secreted by some Elytra. Despite the risks, some "
"value it for its use as a powerful stimulant."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SESettlement03"
msgid ""
"Fellmoor is a small Dementia community of farmers.Their crops have been known "
"to alter a person's sense of reality."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Healer"
msgid ""
"Fighters of poison and illness. The ancient <RT_BlueMed>art of restoration</> "
"is their ally, and the deadly <RT_BlueMed>art of destruction</> is their "
"weapon."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault14"
msgid ""
"Fill your soul gems by soul trapping creatures. You can also soul trap a "
"creature you've summoned."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillDestruction_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Fire, frost and lightning have flowed from your fingertips. You are now a "
"Journeyman in Destruction magic and can cast <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman level "
"Destruction spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillDestruction_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Fire, frost and lightning have flowed from your fingertips. You are now a "
"Master of Destruction magic and can cast <RT_BlueMed>all Destruction "
"spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillDestruction_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Fire, frost and lightning have flowed from your fingertips. You are now an "
"Apprentice in Destruction magic and can cast <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice level "
"Destruction spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillDestruction_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Fire, frost and lightning have flowed from your fingertips. You are now an "
"Expert in Destruction magic and can cast <RT_BlueMed>Expert level Destruction "
"spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMercantile01"
msgid ""
"For an Apprentice of Mercantile, an item's condition does not affect its "
"price."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBravil02"
msgid ""
"For as long as people have lived in Bravil, the statue of the Lucky Old Lady "
"has been considered a symbol of good fortune. Stop by, and the Lady may grant "
"her blessing...."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameChorrol01"
msgid ""
"For his heroism at Pale Pass, Kantus Jeril was appointed the first Count of "
"Chorrol. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault03"
msgid ""
"Giant roots twist across the landscape of Dementia. Its residents and native "
"creatures are similarly twisted, in body and spirit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault07"
msgid ""
"Gnarl are sentient tree-like creatures whose ability to blend into the "
"landscape has surprised many would-be adventurers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE10Load02"
msgid ""
"Golden Saints cast into the waters of Oblivion return to the Shivering Isles "
"through Brellach. The process is considered sacred and secret."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE07Load01"
msgid ""
"Greenmote is a highly addictive and potent drug that can be fatal if not "
"taken in extreme moderation."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault08"
msgid ""
"Grummites are frog-like, tool-making creatures with a primitive culture. They "
"can often be found protecting the egg sacs that house their young."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Khajiit"
msgid ""
"Hailing from the province of Elsweyr, they are <RT_BlueMed>intelligent, "
"quick</> and <RT_BlueMed>agile</>. They make <RT_BlueMed>excellent thieves</> "
"due to their natural agility and <RT_BlueMed>unmatched acrobatics skill</>. "
"All Khajiit <RT_BlueMed>can see in the dark</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SESettlement04"
msgid ""
"Hale is a small Mania community of artists. They believe their art is "
"inspired by the spores from the great mushroom trees that surround their "
"village."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat10"
msgid "Heavier weapons and armor slow you down when you wear them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat05"
msgid "Heavier weapons fatigue you more when you swing them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault11"
msgid ""
"Heretics are fanatics that believe Sheogorath is just a man who needs to be "
"overthrown. They congregate in the lands of Mania."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace05"
msgid ""
"High Elves have the most Magicka, but are also damaged more by all types of "
"magic."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SESettlement05"
msgid ""
"Highcross is a small settlement in the lands of Mania. Its citizens are "
"highly compulsive, acting out bizarre rituals with little meaning."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameAnvil07"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBravil06"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBruma06"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCheydinhal05"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameChorrol06"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity07"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameLeyawiin04"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkingrad04"
msgid ""
"Honest merchants are not interested in stolen goods. Such items do not even "
"appear in the list of goods you wish to sell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault03"
msgid "How people feel about you affects how much information they give you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault09"
msgid ""
"Hungers are Daedric creatures that feed on the misery and despair of "
"everything around them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDialogue08"
msgid ""
"If a topic stays gold in conversation, the character has more to tell you, "
"but only if they like you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth07"
msgid ""
"If the Sneaking eye is open, another character or creature knows you're there."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth06"
msgid "If you are sent to jail, you are able to hide one of your lockpicks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MQ16TempleOfTheOne"
msgid ""
"If you can bring Martin safely into the Temple of the One, there is still a "
"chance to turn defeat into victory."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_ArenaLoad1"
msgid ""
"If you decide to enter the Arena as a combatant, you'd better come prepared. "
"Every match is a fight to the death."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat20"
msgid ""
"If you get into a fight with a friend, you can yield to them to stop the "
"combat by holding Block and interacting with that character. If they like you "
"enough, they will stop the fight."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth01"
msgid ""
"If you sneak up and attack someone who does not detect you, you deal extra "
"damage."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion02"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has a Chameleon spell that makes you partially invisible, but "
"still able to attack and pick up objects."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion04"
msgid "Illusion magic has a Charm spell that makes others like you more."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion03"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has a Command spell that makes others fight to defend you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion08"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has a Paralyze spell that immobilizes your enemy for a short "
"time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion09"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has a Silence spell that prevents your enemy from casting "
"spells."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion06"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has an Invisibility spell that makes you completely invisible. "
"However, it ends when you attack an enemy or use an object."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion01"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has spells that can calm your enemies or give them a killing "
"frenzy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion07"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has spells that can illuminate dark dungeons, or let you see "
"in the dark."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsIllusion05"
msgid ""
"Illusion magic has spells that demoralize your enemies, making them flee, or "
"rally your allies and stop them from fleeing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace08"
msgid ""
"Imperials have the Voice of the Emperor power and can charm others into "
"liking them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellVendor02"
msgid ""
"In Cheydinhal, guild mages favor the College of Alteration. The mages of "
"Bravil prefer the College of Illusion."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Breton"
msgid ""
"In addition to their <RT_BlueMed>quick and perceptive grasp of spellcraft</>, "
"even the humblest of Bretons can <RT_BlueMed>boast a resistance to magical "
"energies</>. They are particularly <RT_BlueMed>skilled at summoning and "
"healing magic</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MS05Dreamworld02"
msgid ""
"In the Dreamworld, your magic and belongings no longer exist, but you still "
"have your talents and skills from the real world."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksCombat01"
msgid ""
"Increasing your Skill level in Blade, Blunt, or Hand-to-Hand improves "
"improves the usefulness of both your Regular and Power Attacks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Chapels05"
msgid ""
"Infamous villains! The Nine may balance the fame of good deeds against the "
"shame of your wickedness when you pray for healing, curing, and restoration "
"at their chapel altars."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE04Load02"
msgid ""
"Ingestion of Felldew results in the release of pheromones that some Elytra "
"recognize, making them indifferent to the user's presence."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault15"
msgid "Ingredients taken from plants grow back after some time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameMagic01"
msgid "Ingredients taken from plants grow back after some time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills02"
msgid "Intelligence determines your total amount of Magicka."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE09Load01"
msgid ""
"It is rumored that screams of agony are carried away on the wind as it passes "
"through Xaselm."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DBSanctuary01"
msgid ""
"It is said that the Count of Cheydinhal knows of the existence of the Dark "
"Brotherhood Sanctuary, but bribes and threats of death have done wonders to "
"keep his mouth shut."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkingrad01"
msgid ""
"Janus Hassildor, Count Skingrad, has ruled Skingrad for many years, and is "
"known by reputation to be a powerful wizard."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDialogue04"
msgid ""
"Joining a faction has great benefits. Everyone in your faction will like you "
"more."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault05"
msgid ""
"Joining the Thieves Guild gives you access to fences who can buy your stolen "
"goods."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat12"
msgid "Jumping, sprinting and fighting decreases your Fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat14"
msgid "Jumping, sprinting and fighting decreases your Fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault01"
msgid "Jumping, sprinting and fighting decreases your Fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DBSanctuary02"
msgid ""
"Just who is the Night Mother? Some say she's an old woman. Others believe "
"she's a spirit or phantom. And there are those still who doubt the Night "
"Mother even exists at all... "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace10"
msgid ""
"Khajiit have the Eye of Fear power, which makes others run in terror from "
"them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE11Load02"
msgid ""
"Knifepoint Hollow is rumored to have once been a great store of knowledge. "
"The details of its history have since fallen into legend."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_KvatchSoldier"
msgid "Kvatch guards"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillArmorer_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Long days and nights at the forge make you strong and tough. You are now a "
"Journeyman Armorer. Using repair hammers, you can now <RT_BlueMed>repair "
"enchanted items</> yourself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillArmorer_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Long days and nights at the forge make you strong and tough. You are now a "
"Master Armorer. Your repair hammers do not wear out while repairing weapons "
"and armor. <RT_BlueMed>One repair hammer lasts you a lifetime</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillArmorer_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Long days and nights at the forge make you strong and tough. You are now an "
"Apprentice Armorer. Your <RT_BlueMed>repair hammers now last twice as long</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillArmorer_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Long days and nights at the forge make you strong and tough. You are now an "
"Expert Armorer. You can now repair items <RT_BlueMed>beyond their maximum "
"durability</>. Improved weapons deal <RT_BlueMed>extra damage</>. Improved "
"armors provide <RT_BlueMed>extra protection</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MS02BenirusManor"
msgid ""
"Lorgren Benirus, who mysteriously disappeared over a hundred years ago, was "
"the original owner of Benirus Manor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault12"
msgid ""
"Madness Ore is often found in ruins of ancient civilizations. It is rumored "
"that a smith in New Sheoth is able to fashion weapons and armor from Madness "
"Ore."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MagesGuild04"
msgid ""
"Mages Guild halls sell Destruction spells in Skingrad, Conjuration in "
"Chorrol, Alteration in Cheydinhal, Illusion in Bravil, Restoration in Anvil, "
"and Mysticism in Leyawiin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellVendor01"
msgid ""
"Mages in the Skingrad guild hall specialize in Destruction, while Chorrol "
"mages specialize in Conjuration."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat19"
msgid ""
"Major Skills are easier to increase, making it a good way to get Experience."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault02"
msgid ""
"Mania is the home of mad artists and creative thinkers. But, do not assume "
"that it is any less dangerous than Dementia."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameLeyawiin01"
msgid ""
"Marius Caro is Count Leyawiin, and his recent bride, the lovely and "
"cultivated Alessia Caro, is the daughter of the righteous and reliable "
"Countess Arriana Valga of Chorrol."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameOblivionGate04"
msgid ""
"Mehrunes Dagon is the daedric prince of destruction, natural disasters, and "
"the bloody scourge."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Spellsword"
msgid ""
"More <RT_BlueMed>nimble and athletic</> than the sorcerer, and better suited "
"for <RT_BlueMed>spell-casting</> than the knight, their attacks are "
"unpredictable. Students of <RT_BlueMed>combat</> and <RT_BlueMed>magic</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsMysticism05"
msgid ""
"Mysticism magic has a Soul Trap spell that traps the spirit energy of a dying "
"enemy in a soul gem. That soul gem can then be used to create or recharge a "
"magic item."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsMysticism06"
msgid ""
"Mysticism magic has a Telekinesis spell that lets you move objects and throw "
"them over great distances."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsMysticism04"
msgid ""
"Mysticism magic has spells that absorb the power of your enemy's spells, "
"adding their Magicka to yours."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsMysticism02"
msgid ""
"Mysticism magic has spells that detect living and undead creatures through "
"walls and other objects."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsMysticism03"
msgid ""
"Mysticism magic has spells that reflect normal attack damage or spells back "
"onto the attacker."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsMysticism01"
msgid "Mysticism magic has spells that remove magic effects from you or others."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Priest"
msgid "NPC class"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Imperial"
msgid ""
"Natives of the civilized, cosmopolitan province of Cyrodiil, they have proved "
"to be <RT_BlueMed>shrewd diplomats and traders</>. They are "
"<RT_BlueMed>skilled with heavy armor and in the social skills</> and tend to "
"favor the warrior classes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMercantile_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Negotiation, bargaining, dickering, haggling, they're all a means to an "
"end... getting the best price for your goods. You are now a Journeyman of "
"Mercantile. You can now buy and sell <RT_BlueMed>any object to any vendor</>, "
"even if they normally do not deal in that type of wares. Merchants may also "
"offer you <RT_BlueMed>even better items</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMercantile_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Negotiation, bargaining, dickering, haggling, they're all a means to an "
"end... getting the best price for your goods. You are now an Apprentice of "
"Mercantile. The damaged condition of an item is <RT_BlueMed>no longer a "
"factor</> when you sell it. Merchants may also offer you <RT_BlueMed>better "
"items</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMercantile_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Negotiation, bargaining, dickering, haggling, they're all a means to an "
"end... getting the best price for your goods. You are now an Expert of "
"Mercantile. All merchants in the world <RT_BlueMed>now have 500 more gold</> "
"available. You can <RT_BlueMed>invest</> in a shop to <RT_BlueMed>permanently "
"increase</> that merchant's <RT_BlueMed>available gold by an additional "
"500</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMercantile_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Negotiation, bargaining, dickering, haggling, they're all a means to an "
"end... getting the best price for your goods. You now always get the "
"<RT_BlueMed>best price possible</> when buying and selling. Merchants now "
"offer you the <RT_BlueMed>best items at their disposal</>. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Charactergen01"
msgid ""
"No one has escaped from the Imperial Prison in over 40 years, since the days "
"of Jagar Tharn and The Imperial Simulacrum."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBruma04"
msgid ""
"Noble heroes! Have your attributes been cursed by the Dark Arts? Seek comfort "
"at the Altar of the Nine at the Bruma Chapel of Talos! Pray, and you shall be "
"restored!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace04"
msgid ""
"Nords are highly resistant to frost attacks, and they have a mighty Shield "
"power which protects them like armor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE08Load02"
msgid ""
"Once a bustling city, Xeddefen has become home to a tribe of Grummites who "
"worship the strange obelisk in the depths of the ruins."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE07Load03"
msgid ""
"Once the home of a great nobleman, the halls of Xirethard are now rife with "
"horrible undead creatures."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace11"
msgid ""
"Orcs have a special Berserk power that temporarily increases their strength, "
"fatigue and health, while draining their agility."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MS12PalePass"
msgid ""
"Pale Pass was the rumored location of the Akaviri headquarters during their "
"invasion of Cyrodiil. The actual location of the fort has been lost over "
"hundreds of years."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SESettlement01"
msgid ""
"Passwall is a small settlement whose residents hope to pass through the Gates "
"of Madness into the greater realm of the Shivering Isles."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault08"
msgid "People don't like it when you talk to them with your weapon drawn."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDialogue07"
msgid "People don't like it when you talk to them with your weapon drawn."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDialogue03"
msgid "People like you less when you make them an offer that they refuse."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills08"
msgid "People like you more if you have a high Personality."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDialogue02"
msgid ""
"People you barter with like you a little bit more each time you make a large "
"transaction with them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSpeechcraft_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Persuasion, wheedling, cajoling, and coercing are all tools of speechcraft. "
"They are tools you seek to excel in. You are now a Master of Speechcraft. "
"When trying to persuade a character, their <RT_BlueMed>disposition no longer "
"decreases</> and Disposition is <RT_BlueMed>less impacted</> by the most "
"disliked action."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSpeechcraft_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Persuasion, wheedling, cajoling, and coercing are all tools of speechcraft. "
"They are tools you seek to excel in. You are now an Apprentice of "
"Speechcraft. When trying to persuade a character, their Disposition now "
"<RT_BlueMed>decreases more slowly</> over time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSpeechcraft_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Persuasion, wheedling, cajoling, and coercing are all tools of speechcraft. "
"They are tools you seek to excel in. You are now an Expert of Speechcraft. "
"When trying to persuade a character, <RT_BlueMed>bribery costs half</> of "
"what it would normally."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSpeechcraft_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Persuasion, wheedling, cajoling, and coercing are all tools of speechcraft. "
"They are tools you seek to excel in. You are now an Journeyman of "
"Speechcraft. When persuading a character, you now get <RT_BlueMed>one chance "
"to rotate the response wedges</> without having to select an action."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCheydinhal03"
msgid ""
"Pilgrims and travelers pray at the Altar of the Nine in Cheydinhal's Chapel "
"of Arkay. Their wounds are healed, their diseases cured, and curses upon "
"their bodies are banished."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE10Load03"
msgid ""
"Pinnacle Rock is the stronghold of the Dark Seducers. Few beyond the Seducers "
"are ever permitted inside."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_VampireDungeonLoad01"
msgid ""
"Porphyric Hemophilia is known as the \"vampire's disease.\" Seek a cure "
"immediately, or you may become a vampire yourself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat13"
msgid ""
"Power attacks do large amounts of damage and are done by holding down the "
"Attack button."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Chapels01"
msgid ""
"Pray in chapels at the Altars of the Nine to rid the body of its afflictions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Mage"
msgid ""
"Prefering to use their extensive <RT_BlueMed>knowledge of all things "
"magical</>, they wield a <RT_BlueMed>might</> more powerful than the sharpest "
"blade."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Scout"
msgid ""
"Preferring the rolling countryside to the city life, they are gifted with the "
"ability to <RT_BlueMed>evade</>, <RT_BlueMed>guard</>, and "
"<RT_BlueMed>protect themselves</> with great proficiency."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Thief"
msgid ""
"Profiting from the losses of others is their love. Able to be "
"<RT_BlueMed>swift in shadow</>, and <RT_BlueMed>crafty in bartering</>. Locks "
"are enemies, and lock-picks are their swords."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault19"
msgid ""
"Purchase a horse to travel faster. You can find them at stables in any city."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MonkAncestorMoth"
msgid ""
"Quick and cunning with the empty hand, they are strong in spirit.  They "
"prefer to solve conflict by arrow or by fist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Widescreen1ElvenArmor"
msgid ""
"Realistic lighting and shader effects combine to create detailed and "
"immersive environments."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace02"
msgid ""
"Redguards have the power of Adrenaline Rush, which allows them to run faster "
"and take damage at increased levels."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat15"
msgid "Resting restores your Health, Magicka, and Fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsRestoration01"
msgid ""
"Restoration magic has spells that absorb Attributes or Skills, temporarily "
"transferring them to you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsRestoration02"
msgid ""
"Restoration magic has spells that absorb Fatigue, Health or Magicka, "
"temporarily transferring them to you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsRestoration03"
msgid ""
"Restoration magic has spells that cure disease and poison. You can even cure "
"paralysis on your allies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsRestoration07"
msgid ""
"Restoration magic has spells that increase your resistance to disease, fire, "
"frost, lightning, magic, normal weapons, paralysis or poison."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsRestoration06"
msgid ""
"Restoration magic has spells that restore damaged attributes, Fatigue, Health "
"or Magicka."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsRestoration04"
msgid ""
"Restoration magic has spells that temporarily increase your Attributes or "
"Skills."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellsRestoration05"
msgid ""
"Restoration magic has spells that temporarily increase your Fatigue, Health "
"or Magicka."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DL9CommuneLoadDoor"
msgid ""
"Rumour claims that Sundercliff Watch was built on the ruins of Varsa Baalim, "
"and inherited the curse of that forgotten Ayleid City."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth08"
msgid ""
"Running is noisier than walking and makes you easier to detect, even if you "
"are sneaking."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault20"
msgid "Sampling raw ingredients can improve your Alchemy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameOblivionGate01"
msgid "Save often. The planes of Oblivion are a dangerous realm."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault05"
msgid "Scalon are hulking swamp creatures with tremendous leaping ability."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSPalaceLoad01"
msgid ""
"Sheogorath is the Daedric Prince of Madness, whose followers include both "
"dangerous psychotics and brilliant artists. His divided personality is "
"reflected in the land itself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSCrucibleLoad03"
msgid ""
"Sheogorath's fiercely loyal Dark Seducers patrol the streets of Crucible. "
"They are aligned with Dementia and are not overly fond of Golden Saints."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksSneak02"
msgid "Sneak Attacks performed by an Apprentice of Sneak deal even more damage."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCreatures01"
msgid ""
"Some creatures, like ghosts, are immune to normal weapons. Use a silver, "
"daedric or magic weapon instead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameAnvil06"
msgid ""
"Some say certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But some "
"officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBravil07"
msgid ""
"Some say certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But some "
"officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBruma07"
msgid ""
"Some say certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But some "
"officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCheydinhal06"
msgid ""
"Some say certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But some "
"officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameChorrol07"
msgid ""
"Some say certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But some "
"officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity08"
msgid ""
"Some say certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But some "
"officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameLeyawiin05"
msgid ""
"Some say certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But some "
"officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkingrad05"
msgid ""
"Some say that certain members of the Thieves Guild will buy stolen goods. But "
"some officials insist the Thieves Guild doesn't even exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SESettlement06"
msgid ""
"Split is a community divided between Mania and Dementia. Its citizens are "
"mirror images of one another, constantly struggling for control of the town."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Guard"
msgid "Standard town guard class."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_GuardBattlemage"
msgid "Standard town guard class."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MS26Guard"
msgid "Standard town guard class."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSneak_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Stepping softly, hiding in the shadows, you do everything in your power to "
"remain undetected. You have become a Journeyman of Sneaking. You now move "
"<RT_BlueMed>more quietly</>, even when <RT_BlueMed>running</> and wearing "
"<RT_BlueMed>heavy boots</>. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSneak_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Stepping softly, hiding in the shadows, you do everything in your power to "
"remain undetected. You have become a Master at Sneaking. While sneaking, any "
"attack on an opponent that has not detected you <RT_BlueMed>ignores their "
"armor.</>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSneak_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Stepping softly, hiding in the shadows, you do everything in your power to "
"remain undetected. You have become an Apprentice of Sneaking. Your Sneak "
"Attacks are now even deadlier."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSneak_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Stepping softly, hiding in the shadows, you do everything in your power to "
"remain undetected. You have become an Expert at Sneaking. You learned how to "
"dissimulate your presence, making you <RT_BlueMed>harder to detect</> in "
"bright environments."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault07"
msgid ""
"Stolen goods in your possession are taken from you when you go to jail. Look "
"for evidence chests in the prisons to get them back."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksMercantile04"
msgid ""
"Stores always have incredible items to barter with a Master of Mercantile."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills01"
msgid ""
"Strength allows you to carry more items and do more damage with most melee "
"weapons."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DL9extLoadDoor"
msgid ""
"Sundercliff Watch was once a waystation during the Reman Dynasty, but has "
"long since faded into disrepair and been all but forgotten."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills11"
msgid "Swimming is better than running to make your Athletics increase."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSCrucibleLoad01"
msgid ""
"Syl is the Lady of Dementia, and Duchess of that land. She is known to be "
"highly paranoid, believing everyone around her to be a potential enemy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSBlissLoad01"
msgid ""
"Thadon is the Lord of Mania, and Duke of that land. He is known to be "
"obsessed with mind-altering food and drink."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCheydinhal02"
msgid ""
"The Abandoned House on the eastern edge of Cheydinhal is never spoken of "
"publicly, and the Count refuses to even acknowledge its existence. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity03"
msgid ""
"The Ayleids, or Heartland High Elves, ruled Cyrodiil in the long ages of Myth "
"before the beginning of recorded history. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault09"
msgid ""
"The Blades are a group of knights who work in secret for the good of the "
"empire."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_ArenaLoad2"
msgid ""
"The Bloodworks beneath the Arena has been appropriately named. Blood often "
"seeps down through the grate of the fighting pit and into this training area."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DBSanctuary03"
msgid ""
"The Cheydinhal Sanctuary is but one of many secret Dark Brotherhood safe "
"havens spread across the Imperial Province. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills05"
msgid ""
"The Clairvoyance spell reveals the path to your next active quest objective."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault17"
msgid ""
"The Conjuration Skill allows you to summon powerful weapons, armor, and "
"creatures to aid you in battle."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills12"
msgid ""
"The Conjuration Skill allows you to summon powerful weapons, armor, and "
"creatures to aid you in battle."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DL9VillageLoadDoor"
msgid ""
"The Drothmeri Army is founded and funded by Frathen Drothan, a rogue arch-"
"mage of the Great House Telvanni."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity01"
msgid ""
"The Elder Council has a long history, stretching back to the founding of the "
"First Empire by Alessia. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_FightersGuild02"
msgid ""
"The Fighters Guild maintains minimum standards of public behavior. You must "
"have a clean criminal record to join."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SETheFringe01"
msgid ""
"The Fringe is an enclosed area designed to test those who wish to enter the "
"Shivering Isles."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE09Load03"
msgid ""
"The Gardens of Flesh and Bone were created by sorceress Relmyna Verenim as "
"her attempt to grow the mystical components of the \"sixth element,\" Flesh."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE02Load01"
msgid ""
"The Gatekeeper guards the Gates of Madness against those not Blessed by "
"Sheogorath."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEGatesMadness01"
msgid ""
"The Gates of Madness serve to keep out casual adventurers. Only those fit for "
"Sheogorath's realm, or those invited, can gain access."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSPalaceLoad03"
msgid ""
"The House of Dementia is renowned for its small cadre of ruthless Dark "
"Seducer Elite Guards."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSPalaceLoad02"
msgid "The House of Mania exemplifies lavishness and over-indulgence."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE11Load03"
msgid ""
"The Howling Halls contain the reconstruction of a famous building from "
"Cyrodiil."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity06"
msgid ""
"The Imperial City Arena attracts gladiators and gamblers from all over "
"Cyrodiil. Risk your gold by betting on a match or your very life as a "
"combatant. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MQ16BattleSpacesLoad"
msgid ""
"The Imperial City is under attack. Martin must reach the Temple of the One or "
"all is lost!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MagesGuild01"
msgid ""
"The Mages Guild is an organization dedicated to the instruction and "
"responsible use of magic throughout the Empire."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MagesGuild02"
msgid ""
"The Mages Guild is committed to rooting out Necromancy and all who practice "
"it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerks01"
msgid ""
"The Magic Schools allow you to learn better spells as you become Apprentice, "
"Journeyman, Expert, and Master in them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault01"
msgid ""
"The Mania region of the Shivering Isles lies to the north. The Dementia "
"region crouches in the south."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Chapels03"
msgid "The Nine love not the wicked, and scorn their prayers at chapel altars."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE03Load02"
msgid ""
"The Resonator of Judgment, made of a material of unknown crystalline origin, "
"is very similar to the strange obelisks that dot the Shivering Isles."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE09Load02"
msgid ""
"The Sanctum of Vivisection is where sorceress Relmyna Verenim lives and "
"conducts her experiments."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE12Load01"
msgid ""
"The Tree of Madness draws its nourishment from the Pools of Mania and "
"Dementia deep beneath the Palace."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth04"
msgid ""
"The amount of light shining on you affects how easy you are to detect. "
"Casting spells can make you easier to see."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE06Load01"
msgid ""
"The ancient city of Cylarne is believed to be the original capital of the "
"Shivering Isles."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_WoodElf"
msgid ""
"The clanfolk of the Western Valenwood forests, also known as \"Bosmer\". Wood "
"Elves are <RT_BlueMed>nimble and quick</>, making them <RT_BlueMed>good "
"scouts and thieves</>, and there are no <RT_BlueMed>finer archers</> in all "
"of Tamriel. Their ability to <RT_BlueMed>command simple creatures</> is well-"
"known."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlade_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"The cuts and nicks from long practice sessions with all manner of blades has "
"its benefits. You are now a Journeyman with Blade weapons. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> now apply <RT_BlueMed>Weakness</> to Normal "
"Weapons."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlade_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"The cuts and nicks from long practice sessions with all manner of blades has "
"its benefits. You are now a Master with Blade weapons. The Weakness to Normal "
"Weapons applied by your <RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> is now even stronger."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlade_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"The cuts and nicks from long practice sessions with all manner of blades has "
"its benefits. You are now an Apprentice with Blade weapons. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> are <RT_BlueMed>more powerful</> and your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Blade weapons</> are <RT_BlueMed>more durable</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlade_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"The cuts and nicks from long practice sessions with all manner of blades has "
"its benefits. You are now an Expert with Blade weapons. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Regular Attacks</> now have a <RT_BlueMed>chance</> to make your "
"opponents <RT_BlueMed>bleed</>, dealing damage over time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_ArenaLoad3"
msgid ""
"The first Arena Blademaster was Gaiden Shinji, a fierce and noble warrior of "
"the Order of Diagna.  "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE32Load01"
msgid ""
"The former settlement of Vitharn is rumored to be haunted by the ghosts of "
"its slaughtered citizens."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MS12PalePassRuins02"
msgid ""
"The fort at Pale Pass was actually an Imperial structure captured and then "
"inhabited by the invading Akaviri forces."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat06"
msgid "The further you are from roads and cities, the greater the danger."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault04"
msgid "The higher the Skill that increases, the more Experience you gain."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_FightersGuild01"
msgid ""
"The highest aspiration of a Fighters Guild member is to advance to the rank "
"of Champion, and eventually Master."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Acrobat"
msgid ""
"The kind of person that uses <RT_BlueMed>Agility and Endurance</> to their "
"advantage. Unafraid of jumping long distances."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_DL9MinesLoadDoor"
msgid ""
"The mines at Sundercliff boast the highest concentration of iron ore in the "
"Valus Mountains."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Knight"
msgid ""
"The most <RT_BlueMed>noble</> of all combatants. <RT_BlueMed>Strong in "
"body</> and <RT_BlueMed>in character</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Redguard"
msgid ""
"The most naturally talented warriors in Tamriel. In addition to their "
"cultural <RT_BlueMed>affinities for many weapon and armor styles</>, they "
"also have a <RT_BlueMed>hardy constitution</> and a <RT_BlueMed>natural "
"resistance to disease and poison</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_ICPalaceGuard"
msgid "The most noble of all combatants.  Strong in body and in character."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMysticism_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"The mysteries of magic are slowly revealing themselves to you. You are now a "
"Journeyman of Mysticism and can cast <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman level Mysticism "
"spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMysticism_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"The mysteries of magic are slowly revealing themselves to you. You are now a "
"Master of Mysticism and can cast <RT_BlueMed>all Mysticism spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMysticism_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"The mysteries of magic are slowly revealing themselves to you. You are now an "
"Apprentice of Mysticism and can cast <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice level Mysticism "
"spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMysticism_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"The mysteries of magic are slowly revealing themselves to you. You are now an "
"Expert of Mysticism and can cast <RT_BlueMed>Expert level Mysticism spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSBlissLoad02"
msgid ""
"The northern half of New Sheoth is named Bliss. Its colorful streets and "
"people are the embodiment of Mania."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Orc"
msgid ""
"The people of the Wrothgarian and Dragontail Mountains, <RT_BlueMed>Orcish "
"armorers</> are prized for their <RT_BlueMed>craftsmanship</>. Orc troops in "
"heavy armor are among the finest in the Empire, and are fearsome when using "
"their <RT_BlueMed>berserker rage</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSBlissLoad03"
msgid ""
"The proud and haughty Golden Saints act as enforcers in Sheogorath's Realm. "
"They are aligned with Mania and are not overly fond of Dark Seducers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameAnvil03"
msgid ""
"The reputable head of the Anvil Mages Guild, Carahil, is an outspoken enemy "
"of necromancy, summoning, and the dark arts."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameLeyawiin02"
msgid ""
"The righteous and godly pray for healing of wounds, for curing of diseases, "
"and for restoration of damaged attributes at the Altar of the Nine at the "
"Leyawiin Chapel of Zenithar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Chapels02"
msgid "The righteous seek blessings from the Nine at altars in the chapels."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillRestoration_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"The secret energies of the human body have not surrendered their mysteries "
"easily to you. You are now a Journeyman of Restoration and can cast "
"<RT_BlueMed>Journeyman level Restoration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillRestoration_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"The secret energies of the human body have not surrendered their mysteries "
"easily to you. You are now a Master of Restoration and can cast "
"<RT_BlueMed>all Restoration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillRestoration_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"The secret energies of the human body have not surrendered their mysteries "
"easily to you. You are now an Apprentice of Restoration and can cast "
"<RT_BlueMed>Apprentice level Restoration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillRestoration_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"The secret energies of the human body have not surrendered their mysteries "
"easily to you. You are now an Expert with Restoration and can cast "
"<RT_BlueMed>Expert level Restoration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE11Load04"
msgid ""
"The secret grove in Milchar can only be accessed by those the grove deems "
"worthy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSBlissLoad04"
msgid "The smith in Bliss can create weapons and armor from Amber."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSCrucibleLoad04"
msgid "The smith in Crucible can mold weapons and armor from Madness Ore."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENSCrucibleLoad02"
msgid ""
"The southern half of New Sheoth is named Crucible. It embodies Dementia, with "
"its ominous buildings and fearful citizens."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSecurity_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"The subtle rattle of lockpicks and falling lock tumblers is music to your "
"ears. Your increased skills have made you a Journeyman of Security. When you "
"pick locks, <RT_BlueMed>only two tumblers now fall when you break a pick</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSecurity_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"The subtle rattle of lockpicks and falling lock tumblers is music to your "
"ears. Your increased skills have made you a Master of Security. When you pick "
"locks, <RT_BlueMed>no tumblers fall when you break a pick</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSecurity_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"The subtle rattle of lockpicks and falling lock tumblers is music to your "
"ears. Your increased skills have made you an Apprentice of Security. When you "
"pick locks, <RT_BlueMed>only three tumblers now fall when you break a pick</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillSecurity_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"The subtle rattle of lockpicks and falling lock tumblers is music to your "
"ears. Your increased skills have made you an Expert of Security. When you "
"pick locks, only <RT_BlueMed>one tumbler now falls when you break a pick</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameChorrol03"
msgid ""
"The symbol of Chorrol is the Great Oak, an ancient tree where the townsfolk "
"gather to share news of the day."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENewSheoth02"
msgid ""
"The teachings of the Manics or the Demented are sermonized at the Sacellum, "
"depending on which faction is currently in favor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlock_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"The truly skillful fighter learns to block with shield and weapon. Diligent "
"practice has made you a Journeyman at Blocking. You now <RT_BlueMed>lose "
"slightly less Fatigue</> when blocking a hit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlock_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"The truly skillful fighter learns to block with shield and weapon. Diligent "
"practice has made you a Master of Blocking. You now <RT_BlueMed>lose a lot "
"less Fatigue</> when blocking a hit. Your <RT_BlueMed>Shield Bash</> now "
"deals <RT_BlueMed>much more damage</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlock_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"The truly skillful fighter learns to block with shield and weapon. Diligent "
"practice has made you an Apprentice at Blocking. Your weapon or shield is "
"<RT_BlueMed>no longer damaged</> by blocking."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlock_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"The truly skillful fighter learns to block with shield and weapon. Diligent "
"practice has made you an Expert at Blocking. You now lose <RT_BlueMed>even "
"less Fatigue</> when blocking a hit. You can also perform a "
"<RT_BlueMed>Shield Bash</> by pressing <IA id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Attack\"/> "
"while blocking to <RT_BlueMed>stagger</> your opponents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMarksman_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"The twang of the bow and the scraping of arrow fletchings are quite familiar "
"to you. As a Master Marksman, your arrows now have a <RT_BlueMed>great chance "
"to paralyze</> your opponents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMarksman_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"The twang of the bow and the scraping of arrow fletchings are quite familiar "
"to you. As a new Apprentice Marksman, <RT_BlueMed>holding the bowstring with "
"a knocked arrow no longer fatigues you</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMarksman_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"The twang of the bow and the scraping of arrow fletchings are quite familiar "
"to you. As a new Journeyman Marksman, you can now focus your vision to "
"<RT_BlueMed>aim more precisely</> by holding <IA "
"id=\"IA_Game_Combat_Block\"/>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillMarksman_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"The twang of the bow and the scraping of arrow fletchings are quite familiar "
"to you. As an Expert Marksman, your arrows now have a <RT_BlueMed>slight "
"chance to paralyze</> your opponents. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth03"
msgid "The weight of your boots affects how well you can sneak."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SENewSheoth01"
msgid ""
"There are no jails in the Shivering Isles. Criminals are temporarily exiled "
"to a dungeon, instead. If they get out alive, their crimes are forgiven."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameOblivionGate02"
msgid "There are sixteen daedra princes, each with his own plane of Oblivion."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE11Load01"
msgid ""
"There is a chamber in Knifepoint Hollow that has been sealed for millennia. "
"Few but Sheogorath knows who or what is imprisoned there."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth02"
msgid ""
"There's a small chance that being locked in jail will increase your Security "
"or Sneak Skill."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Rogue"
msgid ""
"They use <RT_BlueMed>speed</> in combat rather than brute force. "
"<RT_BlueMed>Persuasive</> in conversation, their tongues are as sharp as "
"blades."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHandToHand_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Thick calluses cover your knuckles and joints from long hours of punching and "
"kicking. At long last you are a Journeyman in Hand-to-Hand combat. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> now have a slight chance to "
"<RT_BlueMed>disarm</> your opponents and your fists can now hit creatures "
"<RT_BlueMed>immune to physical attacks</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHandToHand_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Thick calluses cover your knuckles and joints from long hours of punching and "
"kicking. At long last you are a Master of Hand-to-Hand combat. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Regular Attacks</> now inflict <RT_BlueMed>even more Fatigue "
"damage</>. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHandToHand_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Thick calluses cover your knuckles and joints from long hours of punching and "
"kicking. At long last you are an Apprentice in Hand-to-Hand combat. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> are now <RT_BlueMed>more powerful</> and "
"blocking with your fists always makes your opponents <RT_BlueMed>recoil</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillHandToHand_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Thick calluses cover your knuckles and joints from long hours of punching and "
"kicking. You are now an Expert in Hand-to-Hand combat. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Regular Attacks</> now inflict <RT_BlueMed>more Fatigue damage</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_ABAT"
msgid "This is the big description for Absorb Attribute."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Argonian"
msgid ""
"This reptilian race, well-suited for the treacherous swamps of its homeland, "
"has developed <RT_BlueMed>natural immunities to poisons</>. They can "
"<RT_BlueMed>breathe under water</> and are <RT_BlueMed>good at picking "
"locks</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignApprentice"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Apprentice have an <RT_BlueMed>increased "
"amount of Magicka</>, but are also <RT_BlueMed>more susceptible to magical "
"attacks</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Magicka</>: Increases Magicka by 100 points.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Weakness to Magic</>: Increases susceptibility to magic by 100%."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign02"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Apprentice have increased Magicka, but also "
"have a weakness to it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignAtronach"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Atronach <RT_BlueMed>cannot regenerate "
"Magicka</>, but have the ability to <RT_BlueMed>absorb</> any "
"<RT_BlueMed>magic</> cast at them.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Magicka</>: Increases Magicka by 150 points.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Spell Absorption</>: 50% chance of absorbing spells cast at "
"them.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Stunted Magicka</>: Magicka regeneration is halted."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign12"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Atronach cannot regenerate Magicka, but have "
"a chance of absorbing any magic cast at them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignLady"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Lady benefit from increased "
"<RT_BlueMed>Willpower</> and <RT_BlueMed>Endurance</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Willpower</>: Increases Willpower by 10 points.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Endurance</>: Increases Endurance by 10 points."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign06"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Lady have increased Willpower and Endurance."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignLord"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Lord are <RT_BlueMed>more resistant to "
"physical and magic damage</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Shield</>: Increases Armor Rating by 15.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Resist Magic</>: Increases magic resistance by 15%."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign07"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Lord are more resistant to magic and "
"physical damage."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignLover"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Lover can <RT_BlueMed>paralyze</> "
"others.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Lover's Kiss (greater power)</>: Paralyzes the target for 10 "
"seconds and reduces the caster's fatigue by 120 points. Can be used once per "
"day."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign09"
msgid "Those born under the sign of The Lover can paralyze others with a kiss."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignMage"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Mage have an <RT_BlueMed>increased amount of "
"Magicka</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Magicka</>: Increases Magicka by 50 points."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign01"
msgid "Those born under the sign of The Mage have increased Magicka."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignRitual"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Ritual can <RT_BlueMed>heal</> themselves "
"and <RT_BlueMed>make the undead flee in horror</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Blessed Word</>: Forces the undead to flee in horror for 30 "
"seconds. Can be used multiple times per day at a cost of 40 Magicka points "
"per cast.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Mara's Gift (greater power)</>: Restores 200 points of health. "
"Can be used once per day."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign03"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Ritual can heal themselves and turn the "
"undead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignSerpent"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Serpent can <RT_BlueMed>poison others</>, "
"though it comes at the cost of damaging their own Fatigue.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Serpent Spell (greater power)</>: Deal 3 points of damage for "
"20 seconds. It also cures Poison, dispels 90 points and damage Fatigue 100 "
"points to the caster. Can be used once per day."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign13"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Serpent can poison others at a loss of their "
"own Fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignShadow"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Shadow can become "
"<RT_BlueMed>invisible</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Moonshadow (greater power)</>: Grants invisibility for 60 "
"seconds. Can be used once per day."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign10"
msgid "Those born under the sign of The Shadow can make themselves invisible."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignSteed"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Steed can <RT_BlueMed>move faster</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Speed</>: Increases movement speed by 20 points."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign05"
msgid "Those born under the sign of The Steed can move faster."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignThief"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Thief benefit from increased "
"<RT_BlueMed>Agility</>, <RT_BlueMed>Speed</> and <RT_BlueMed>Luck</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Agility</>: Increases Agility by 10 points.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Luck</>: Increases Luck by 10 points.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Speed</>: Increases Speed by 10 points."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign08"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Thief have increased Agility, Speed, and "
"Luck."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignTower"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Tower can magically <RT_BlueMed>unlock "
"doors</> and <RT_BlueMed>reflect damage</> from their attackers.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Tower Key</>: Opens locks of average difficulty. Can be used "
"once per day.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Tower Warden (greater power)</>: Reflects 5% of all incoming "
"damage for 120 seconds. Can be used once per day."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign11"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Tower can unlock doors magically, and the "
"Tower Warden power reflects damage from attackers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_BirthSignWarrior"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Warrior benefit from increased "
"<RT_BlueMed>Strength</> and <RT_BlueMed>Endurance</>.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Endurance</>: Increases Endurance by 10 points.\n"
"\n"
"• <RT_BlueMed>Fortify Strength</>: Increases Strength by 10 points."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBirthsign04"
msgid ""
"Those born under the sign of The Warrior have increased Strength and "
"Endurance."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksAthletics01"
msgid "Those skilled in Athletics use less Fatigue to sprint."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameBravil04"
msgid ""
"Those with damaged Strength, Agility, Personality, or other attributes pray "
"at the Altar of the Nine at Bravil's Chapel of Mara for restoration."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault12"
msgid ""
"Though Nibenese in speech and custom, Bruma and Cheydinhal show Nord and Dark "
"Elf influences in their architecture."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillConjuration_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Through steady practice you have discovered more creatures to summon from the "
"planes of Oblivion. You are now a Journeyman in Conjuration magic and can "
"cast <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman level Conjuration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillConjuration_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Through steady practice you have discovered more creatures to summon from the "
"planes of Oblivion. You are now a Master of Conjuration magic and can cast "
"<RT_BlueMed>all Conjuration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillConjuration_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Through steady practice you have discovered more creatures to summon from the "
"planes of Oblivion. You are now an Apprentice in Conjuration magic and can "
"cast <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice level Conjuration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillConjuration_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Through steady practice you have discovered more creatures to summon from the "
"planes of Oblivion. You are now an Expert in Conjuration magic and can cast "
"<RT_BlueMed>Expert level Conjuration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault18"
msgid ""
"To level up, find a bed to sleep in. Beds can be found in rooms for rent in "
"Taverns. You can also find bedrolls in wilderness camps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault06"
msgid ""
"To perform Alchemy, you must have at least a Mortar and Pestle. Adding a "
"Calcinator, Alembic or Retort helps improve your potions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Warrior"
msgid ""
"Unafraid of <RT_BlueMed>light weaponry</>, they plow into the fray with "
"little regard for injury. <RT_BlueMed>Masters of all melee tools</>, they put "
"little faith in the magical arts."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_Charactergen03"
msgid ""
"Uriel Septim is a direct descendent of Tiber Septim, who conquered all of "
"Cyrodiil and proclaimed himself Emperor in 2E846."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat04"
msgid "Use Repair Hammers to repair your armor and weapons."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameMagic05"
msgid ""
"Varla Stones found in Ayleid Ruins can be used to recharge your magic items."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameStealth05"
msgid "Watch what you pick up. People don't like it when you steal their goods."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDefault02"
msgid ""
"Watch what you pick up. Your bounty goes up if someone catches you stealing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameMagic03"
msgid "Wearing armor you are not skilled in reduces your magic effectiveness."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameMagic04"
msgid ""
"Welkynd Stones found in Ayleid Ruins can be used to regenerate your Magicka."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerksAthletics02"
msgid ""
"When in combat, manage your Fatigue well as running out of it might get you "
"staggered or knocked down."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills10"
msgid ""
"When you raise your level, your Health scales accordingly to your Endurance."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameImperialCity02"
msgid ""
"White Gold Tower, built many ages ago by ancient Ayleids, can be seen from "
"any part of the Imperial City."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAthletics_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Why jog when you can sprint has always been your motto. Now the miles of "
"running and hours of swimming have paid off. You are a Journeyman of "
"Athletics. Sprinting now consumes <RT_BlueMed>slightly less Fatigue</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAthletics_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Why jog when you can sprint has always been your motto. Now the miles of "
"running and hours of swimming have paid off. You are a Master of Athletics. "
"Sprinting <RT_BlueMed>no longer consumes any Fatigue</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAthletics_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Why jog when you can sprint has always been your motto. Now the miles of "
"running and hours of swimming have paid off. You are an Apprentice of "
"Athletics. You <RT_BlueMed>no longer regenerate less Fatigue</> while running."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAthletics_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Why jog when you can sprint has always been your motto. Now the miles of "
"running and hours of swimming have paid off. You are an Expert of Athletics. "
"Sprinting now consumes <RT_BlueMed>a lot less Fatigue</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkills04"
msgid "Willpower greatly affects your total amount of Fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameRace07"
msgid ""
"Wood Elves can command other creatures to fight for them with their Beast "
"Tongue power."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE03Load01"
msgid ""
"Xedilian, once a main line of defense for the Shivering Isles, was abandoned "
"after the Gatekeeper was created."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SE07Load02"
msgid ""
"Xirethard's proximity to the House of Dementia makes it ideal for an "
"underground emergency escape route."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_MagesGuild03"
msgid ""
"You can join the Mages Guild by visiting a guild hall in any major city. "
"However, entrance to the Arcane University in the Imperial City is granted "
"only to higher ranked members."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameDialogue06"
msgid "You can make new friends, and enemies, by joining a faction."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat17"
msgid ""
"You can regain your Health, Magicka and Fatigue quickly by waiting or "
"sleeping, as long as there are no enemies around. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat11"
msgid "You can run faster with your weapon sheathed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameMagic02"
msgid "You can soul trap creatures that you summon yourself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat18"
msgid ""
"You can use books, ingredients, torches, potions, apparatuses and repair "
"hammers by selecting them in your inventory or assigning them to the quick "
"wheel. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameMagic06"
msgid ""
"You can view magic, abilities, and diseases that are affecting you from the "
"Active Effects page in your magic menu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlunt_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"You have lumps and bruises from long practice sessions with all kinds of "
"maces and axes. You are now a Journeyman with Blunt weapons. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> temporarily grant you <RT_BlueMed> Shield</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlunt_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"You have lumps and bruises from long practice sessions with all kinds of "
"maces and axes. You are now a Master with Blunt weapons. The "
"<RT_BlueMed>Shield</> granted by your <RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> is now "
"even stronger."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlunt_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"You have lumps and bruises from long practice sessions with all kinds of "
"maces and axes. You are now an Apprentice with Blunt weapons. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Power Attacks</> are <RT_BlueMed>more powerful</> and your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Blunt weapons</> are <RT_BlueMed>more durable</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillBlunt_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"You have lumps and bruises from long practice sessions with all kinds of "
"maces and axes. You are now an Expert with Blunt weapons. Your "
"<RT_BlueMed>Regular Attacks</> now have a chance to <RT_BlueMed>silence</> "
"your opponents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlteration_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"You have unlocked more arcane secrets of altering the fabric of reality. You "
"can now cast <RT_BlueMed>Apprentice level Alteration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlteration_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"You have unlocked more arcane secrets of altering the fabric of reality. You "
"can now cast <RT_BlueMed>Expert level alteration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlteration_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"You have unlocked more arcane secrets of altering the fabric of reality. You "
"can now cast <RT_BlueMed>Journeyman level Alteration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlteration_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"You have unlocked more arcane secrets of altering the fabric of reality. You "
"can now cast <RT_BlueMed>all Alteration spells</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCombat16"
msgid "You must find a bed and rest to raise your level."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSkingrad02"
msgid ""
"You need your wounds healed? Your diseases cured? Your attributes restored? "
"Go to the Skingrad Chapel of Julianos and pray at the Altar of the Nine."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameSpellVendor03"
msgid ""
"You'll find Restoration spells at the Anvil Mages Guild, and Mysticism spells "
"in Leyawiin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameOblivionGate03"
msgid ""
"You'll find rare ingredients in the planes of Oblivion that may prove useful "
"when performing Alchemy."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGameCheydinhal01"
msgid ""
"You'll find the best quality horses at the Black Waterside Stables in "
"Cheydinhal."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_InGamePerks02"
msgid "Your Alchemy level determines the effects you can gain from ingredients."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillLightArmor_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Your light armor is like a second skin after all those days and weeks wearing "
"it. You have learned to move easily with it in combat. As a Journeyman of "
"Light Armor, <RT_BlueMed>your gear is now damaged at a lower rate</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillLightArmor_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Your light armor is like a second skin after all those days and weeks wearing "
"it. You have learned to move easily with it in combat. As a Master of Light "
"Armor, your <RT_BlueMed>protection is greatly increased</> when wearing "
"<RT_BlueMed>only Light armor gear</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillLightArmor_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Your light armor is like a second skin after all those days and weeks wearing "
"it. You have learned to move easily with it in combat. As an Apprentice of "
"Light Armor, <RT_BlueMed>your gear is now damaged at a normal rate</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillLightArmor_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Your light armor is like a second skin after all those days and weeks wearing "
"it. You have learned to move easily with it in combat. As an Expert of Light "
"Armor, <RT_BlueMed>your gear no longer encumbers you</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlchemy_LEVEL1"
msgid ""
"Your stained fingers attest to your diligence in mixing potions and learning "
"their secrets. You are now a Journeyman of Alchemy. You now recognize an "
"<RT_BlueMed>additional alchemical property</>, and can sustain "
"<RT_BlueMed>more simultaneous potion effects</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlchemy_LEVEL3"
msgid ""
"Your stained fingers attest to your diligence in mixing potions and learning "
"their secrets. You are now a Master of Alchemy. You can now "
"<RT_BlueMed>create potions from a single ingredient</> and can sustain "
"<RT_BlueMed>even more simultaneous potion effects</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlchemy_LEVEL0"
msgid ""
"Your stained fingers attest to your diligence in mixing potions and learning "
"their secrets. You are now an Apprentice of Alchemy. You now recognize an "
"<RT_BlueMed>additional alchemical property</>, and can <RT_BlueMed>sometimes "
"craft an additional potion</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SkillAlchemy_LEVEL2"
msgid ""
"Your stained fingers attest to your diligence in mixing potions and learning "
"their secrets. You are now an Expert of Alchemy. You now recognize all "
"<RT_BlueMed>additional alchemical properties</>, and are "
"<RT_BlueMed>guaranteed to craft an additional potion</>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ST_Descriptions/LOC_DE_SEInGameDefault10"
msgid ""
"Zealots are fanatical believers in a cult of Sheogorath, and will not "
"tolerate anyone that does not share their beliefs. They congregate in the "
"lands of Dementia."
msgstr ""

